{"format":"bbdb","version":1,"name":"Default","exportedAt":"2026-10-20T17:13:16.083Z","files":{"wrestlers.json":[{"id":1,"name":"Aron Stevens","realName":"Aron Stevens","nickname":"","type":"manager","promotionId":79,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":242,"height":190,"dateOfBirth":"1982-04-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":18,"charisma":69,"micSkills":66,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":98,"ability":59,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":51,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"To see Damien Sandow in action was like watching a kaleidoscope in human form: He stuck and moved, avoiding stagnation and keeping opponents guessing as to how — or whom — he would attack.\r\n\r\nAs a snooty brute in a blue robe, he connived his way to a Money in the Bank contract and nearly took the World Heavyweight Championship from John Cena. Next, as master mimic Damien Mizdow, he stormed from under The Miz’s shadow to steal the spotlight (and earn the WWE Tag Team Titles for the pair). And, as “Macho Mandow,” he briefly resurrected the spirit of one of the most beloved WWE Hall of Famers in history.\r\n\r\nWas it madness? Perhaps. However, Sandow’s willingness to take the ball and run with it endeared him to the WWE Universe, who cheered his dogged determination.","alterEgos":["Aron Rex","Damien Mizdow","Damien Sandow","Macho Mandow"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1","wrestlerId":1,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2019-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1221,1295,1466,2002,2744,2927,2928,3078],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":77,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Damien Sandow.png"},{"id":2,"name":"Santino Marella","realName":"Santino Marella","nickname":"","type":"manager","promotionId":28,"base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":233,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1974-03-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":30,"charisma":59,"micSkills":74,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":42,"potentialAbility":44,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Anthony Carelli, best known by his WWE ring name Santino Marella, is an Italian-Canadian professional wrestler. Carelli started his career on the Ontario independent circuit as Johnny GeoBasco, debuting with a disqualification win over Xhibit (now Rico Montana) in the opening match of a Ring Wars show in Orangeville, Ontario, on August 17, 2003. In the second half of 2004, Carelli wrestled four matches for BattlARTS in Japan, as Joe Basko. In 2005, Carelli (as Johnny Geo Basco) began training at Ohio Valley Wrestling (OVW), a developmental territory for World Wrestling Entertainment (WWE). In July, during a storyline where he was supposed to act afraid of The Boogeyman, but instead laughed, Carelli was shouted at and slapped by Jim Cornette, OVW's head booker and co-owner.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mississauga, Ontario, Canada","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2","wrestlerId":2,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2023-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":77,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":82,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":75,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"Santino Marella.png"},{"id":3,"name":"AJ Lee","realName":"AJ Mendez","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":115,"height":154,"dateOfBirth":"1987-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":75000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":53,"charisma":28,"micSkills":45,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":100,"ability":34,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":58,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"April Jeanette Mendez is an American professional wrestler. Shortly after leaving university Mendez researched wrestling schools and enrolled in one a mile away from her house. To pay the tuition she began working full-time and became an official student in March 2007, debuting six months later as \"Miss April\" to work the New Jersey independent wrestling circuit. On October 10, 2008, Miss April made her debut for Women Superstars Uncensored (WSU). Mendez signed a contract with World Wrestling Entertainment on May 5, 2009, and was assigned to Florida Championship Wrestling, WWE's developmental territory. AJ made her main roster debut on the May 27, 2011, episode of SmackDown when she and Kaitlyn (known as The Chickbusters) lost to the team of Alicia Fox and Tamina.","alterEgos":["AJ Mendez"],"birthplace":"Union City, New Jersey, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-3","wrestlerId":3,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2025-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":75000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1405],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":78,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":71,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"picture":"AJ Lee.png"},{"id":5,"name":"Arn Anderson","realName":"Arn Anderson","nickname":"","type":"manager","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":255,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1958-09-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1982-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":29,"charisma":71,"micSkills":66,"condition":47,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":78,"ability":72,"currentAbility":33,"potentialAbility":33,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Arn Anderson is a retired American wrestler who works as a manager and a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, WCW and AEW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He was one half of the Tag Team Of The Year in 1991. He is part of the WWE Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2697,2698,3270],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":91,"storytelling":94,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":95,"psychology":91,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":28,"technicalCoaching":20,"characterCoaching":73,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":28,"consistency":75,"awareness":91,"judgement":95},"picture":"Arn Anderson.png"},{"id":6,"name":"B.G. James","realName":"B.G. James","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":241,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1969-05-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":35,"charisma":40,"micSkills":33,"condition":52,"hardcoreAbility":9,"injuryProne":100,"ability":22,"currentAbility":13,"potentialAbility":13,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Brian Girard \"B.G.\" James is an American professional wrestler and former United States Marine. James is best known for his appearances with the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) as The Roadie from 1994 to 1995 and as \"The Road Dogg\" Jesse James or simply Road Dogg from 1996 to 2001. He is also known for his appearances with Total Nonstop Action Wrestling as B.G. James from 2002 to 2009, and has also made appearances for several other promotions such as Smoky Mountain Wrestling, World Championship Wrestling, the United States Wrestling Association, the Catch Wrestling Association, and World Wrestling All-Stars. James has held numerous championships over the course of his career, including the WWF Intercontinental Championship once, the WWF Tag Team Championship five times with Billy Gunn as the New Age Outlaws, the WWF Hardcore Championship once, and the NWA World Tag Team Championship twice with Konnan and Ron Killings under the Freebird Rule as the 3Live Kru.","alterEgos":["Road Dogg"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[909,910,1246,1560,2777,2799],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":47,"storytelling":56,"productFit":47,"riskTaking":39,"matchLayout":90,"psychology":89,"workerManagement":95,"trainingIntensity":50,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":28,"teaching":59,"diagnosis":42,"rehabilitation":27,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":46,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":21,"ruleKnowledge":51,"positioning":41,"reactionSpeed":33,"consistency":27,"awareness":58,"judgement":57},"picture":"BG James_alt4.png"},{"id":8,"name":"Billy Kidman","realName":"Billy Kidman","nickname":"","type":"writer","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":195,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1974-05-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":8,"charisma":80,"micSkills":98,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":100,"ability":86,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Peter Alan Gruner, Jr. is an American professional wrestler, trainer, and wrestling producer, better known by his ring name Billy Kidman. Kidman is best known for his work with World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and WWE throughout the late 1990s, early to late 2000s, and the early 2010s. He trained the likes of Wade Barrett in Florida Championship Wrestling. He joined World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and ultimately gained fame as a key member of several strong wrestling factions. In addition to being a member of Raven's Flock, he also was a member of the Filthy Animals and later The New Blood. As a member of these factions, Gruner participated in memorable rivalries with top WCW names, including Hulk Hogan, Jeff Jarrett, and Rey Mysterio. Kidman wrestled for WCW for many years and won tag team gold with partner and real life friend Mysterio. After leaving the group, he won the WCW Cruiserweight Championship three times.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"New Haven, Connecticut, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-8","wrestlerId":8,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2010-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1422,2750,2751],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":34,"characterCoaching":40,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":40,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":27,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":58,"awareness":72,"judgement":83},"picture":"Billy Kidman_alt2.png"},{"id":9,"name":"Booker T","realName":"Booker T","nickname":"","type":"commentator","promotionId":65,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":256,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1965-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":41,"charisma":43,"micSkills":49,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"ability":43,"currentAbility":22,"potentialAbility":22,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Can you dig it? Booker T is an 11-time WCW Tag Team Champion, a six-time World Champion, winner of the 2006 King of the Ring Tournament and the man responsible for popularizing the word, “Sucka!” in sports-entertainment. He also bears the distinction of holding the WCW World Heavyweight Championship when the promotion folded in 2001.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment he stepped into the WWE ring, Booker T Spinaroonied his way into Superstardom, tangling with a who’s who of squared circle greats, including “Stone Cold” Steve Austin, The Undertaker, John Cena, Triple H, Randy Orton, Batista, Rey Mysterio, Ric Flair, Christian, Mark Henry and many others.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-9","wrestlerId":9,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2022-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2714,3285],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":35,"characterCoaching":81,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":81,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":62,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"picture":"Booker T.png"},{"id":11,"name":"Bret Hart","realName":"Bret Hart","nickname":"","type":"scout","base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":235,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1957-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1978-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":58,"charisma":97,"micSkills":88,"condition":47,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":42,"ability":100,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":46,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Bret Hart is a Canadian writer, actor, and retired professional wrestler. A member of the Hart wrestling family, Hart has an amateur wrestling background, wrestling at Ernest Manning High School and Mount Royal College. Along with his \"Hitman\" nickname, Hart was known by the monikers \"The Excellence of Execution\", \"The Best There Is, The Best There Was, and The Best There Ever Will Be\" and \"The Pink and Black Attack\". Hart joined his father Stu Hart's promotion Stampede Wrestling in 1976, made his in-ring debut in 1978. He gained popularity and championship success throughout the 1980s and 1990s in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE), where he helmed The Hart Foundation faction. He left for World Championship Wrestling (WCW) following the controversial \"Montreal Screwjob\" in November 1997, where he remained until October 2000 when he retired following a concussion, achieving much success despite his creative handling being widely criticized.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Canada","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1093],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":39,"storytelling":35,"productFit":45,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":31,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":24,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":32,"characterCoaching":26,"teaching":22,"diagnosis":45,"rehabilitation":42,"prevention":41,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":26,"ruleKnowledge":41,"positioning":22,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":44,"awareness":34,"judgement":88},"picture":"Bret Hart_alt1.png"},{"id":12,"name":"Brian Myers","realName":"Brian Myers","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":28,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":223,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1985-04-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":20,"charisma":70,"micSkills":86,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":100,"ability":71,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":74,"morale":"poor","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"There have been some legendary streaks in sports-entertainment history, but no Superstar can touch the streak held by Curt Hawkins — 269 consecutive losses without a single win. \r\n\r\nOf course, there's much more to Hawkins than a couple hundred consecutive L's. One of the rare Superstars who can claim to be a veteran without a single gray hair, Hawkins has been competing in WWE since 2007 when he backed up Edge alongside Zack Ryder as the lookalike Edgeheads. The pair not only claimed the WWE Tag Team Titles during this time, but mixed it up with The Undertaker in the main event of WrestleMania XXIV when their mentor took on The Deadman.","alterEgos":["Curt Hawkins"],"birthplace":"Glen Cove, New York, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-12","wrestlerId":12,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2020-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[961,1419,2660,3409,3494,3811,4001],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":10,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":90,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":86,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"Brian Myers.png"},{"id":13,"name":"Brock Lesnar","realName":"Brock Lesnar","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":286,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1977-07-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":80,"charisma":70,"micSkills":73,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":95,"morale":"excellent","presentation":"face","prestige":"high","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Glory to The Conqueror, The Beast Incarnate, The Anomaly or whatever godlike title you choose to bestow upon Brock Lesnar. Surely, this creature fits each and every one of them.\r\n\r\nPossessing the type of staggering strength and frightening intensity seen only among Superman villains, this 6-foot-3, 266-pound freak of nature from Minneapolis, Minn., has forced his way to the top of every major combat sport. He won the NCAA Division I collegiate wrestling championship as a senior at the University of Minnesota, the WWE Championship within six months of his debut and the UFC Heavyweight Title in his fourth professional MMA fight. He also became The One in 21-1. Plain and simple, the man was built to destroy.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1225],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":55,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":84,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":45,"mediaHandling":84,"brandBuilding":96,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":62,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"picture":"Brock Lesnar_alt7.png"},{"id":14,"name":"Bryan Danielson","realName":"Bryan Danielson","nickname":"","type":"commentator","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":196,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1981-05-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":64,"charisma":38,"micSkills":39,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":15,"injuryProne":95,"ability":45,"currentAbility":36,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Bryan Danielson is a retired American wrestler who works as a colour commentator and a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, CMLL, NJPW, NOAH, PWG and ROH. He is married to Brie Garcia. He is part of the ROH Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":["Daniel Bryan","Infinito"],"birthplace":"Aberdeen, Washington, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-14","wrestlerId":14,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2021-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[259,1359,1892,2752,3459],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":91,"storytelling":92,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":92,"psychology":91,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":92,"technicalCoaching":92,"characterCoaching":85,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":92,"consistency":91,"awareness":91,"judgement":95},"picture":"Bryan Danielson.png"},{"id":15,"name":"Kaitlyn","realName":"Kaitlyn","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":128,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1986-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":10,"charisma":41,"micSkills":45,"condition":98,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"ability":37,"currentAbility":33,"potentialAbility":33,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Celeste Beryl Bonin is an American body builder, model, and professional wrestler better known by her ring name, Kaitlyn. In July 2010, Bonin signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Entertainment, and was assigned to Florida Championship Wrestling (FCW), WWE's developmental territory. In September 2010, she competed in the all-female third season of NXT where she made her mark by feuding with her Pro Vickie Guerrero, and went on to win the competition in November 2010, thus becoming the only female in history to have won NXT. Prior to her debut to the main roster in December 2010, she formed a tag team with AJ known as The Chickbusters in May 2011. After the split of the team in May 2012, she returned to singles competition, and started to become known as \"The Hybrid Diva of the WWE\" (combination of beauty and power).","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1405],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":47,"productFit":30,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":48,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":30,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":32,"characterCoaching":57,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":56,"awareness":42,"judgement":37},"picture":"Kaitlyn_alt7.png"},{"id":16,"name":"Chad Patton","realName":"Chad Patton","nickname":"","type":"referee","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":169,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1976-05-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":5,"charisma":82,"micSkills":92,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":82,"injuryProne":98,"ability":75,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":55,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Chad Patton was first introduced to the WWE family by friend, Jack Doan. On his days off and on the weekend, Patton would help set up the ring for WWE events in the Midwest. Officials recognized his hard work and put him in charge of putting up the stage. Eventually, it became a full-time job for Patton. At one point, he was asked to try his hand at ring announcing, which Patton says he was terrible at. Patton was thrilled when a referee position became available and tried out. He's been a WWE referee ever since.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-16","wrestlerId":16,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2005-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":0,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":0,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":0,"ruleKnowledge":84,"positioning":67,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Chad Patton_alt1.png"},{"id":17,"name":"Charles Robinson","realName":"Charles Robinson","nickname":"","type":"referee","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":150,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1964-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":11,"charisma":100,"micSkills":79,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":97,"injuryProne":96,"ability":95,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Charles Shane Robinson is an American professional wrestling referee. While growing up, Robinson idolized NWA superstar Ric Flair. He also studied NWA referee Tommy Young in order to hone his mannerisms as a referee. His professional wrestling career began when he joined the Pro Wrestling Federation (PWF) as a photographer in 1993, supplementing his income by working as a salesman. After being used as a special guest referee, he later became a full-time referee for the PWF. Robinson repeatedly petitioned the World Championship Wrestling (WCW) professional wrestling promotion for a job. In 1997, after working with Dan Hedman as a professional sales representative, he was given a tryout match, referreeing a dark match between Chris Taylor and a jobber. Following the match, Robinson was signed to a contract by WCW. In 1999, Robinson became the heel referee of the Four Horsemen, aligning himself with his hero, Ric Flair.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-17","wrestlerId":17,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":35,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":35,"brandBuilding":18,"socialMediaSavvy":18,"ruleKnowledge":94,"positioning":75,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":80,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Charles Robinson_alt1.png"},{"id":18,"name":"Chris Jericho","realName":"Chris Jericho","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":227,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1970-11-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":64,"charisma":79,"micSkills":90,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":87,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"technical","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Chris Jericho is a Canadian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a 5'11\", 227lb worker who is classed as using a Regular style. He uses the Code Breaker, the Judas Effect and the Walls of Jericho as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NJPW, WCW, CMLL and ECW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He has been voted Male Wrestler Of The Year three times. He has been voted Male Veteran Wrestler Of The Year three times. Outside of wrestling he is a relatively well known musician.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Manhasset, New York, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-18","wrestlerId":18,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[584,1114,2663,2701,3822,3928],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":87,"storytelling":89,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":89,"psychology":87,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":88,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":88,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":85,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":58,"awareness":87,"judgement":92},"picture":"Chris Jericho.png"},{"id":19,"name":"Claudio Castagnoli","realName":"Claudio Castagnoli","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"Europe","gender":"M","weight":242,"height":193,"dateOfBirth":"1980-12-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":48,"charisma":70,"micSkills":74,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"ability":70,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":82,"morale":"fair","pres