"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Austin Aries is an American wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a 5'9\", 202lb worker who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He uses the 450° Splash, the Brainbuster and the Last Chancery as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, CMLL, TNA, NXT, ROH, NWA and MLW. He is currently the MLW National Openweight champion.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2027-04-05T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-109","wrestlerId":109,"promotionId":68,"startDate":"2025-04-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-04-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":19700,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1026,1074,1270,2752],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":82,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":71,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":73,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"picture":"Austin Aries_alt4.png"},{"id":110,"name":"Brian Hebner","realName":"Brian Hebner","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":169,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1978-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":4,"charisma":0,"micSkills":0,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":14,"injuryProne":93,"ability":0,"currentAbility":0,"potentialAbility":2,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Brian Hebner is an American man who tends to stay behind the scenes in the wrestling world.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":35,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":35,"brandBuilding":8,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":80,"positioning":64,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":55,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Brian Hebner_alt2.png"},{"id":113,"name":"Brother Devon","realName":"Brother Devon","nickname":"","type":"trainer","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":269,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1972-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":34,"charisma":93,"micSkills":92,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":100,"ability":82,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Devon E. Hughes is an American professional wrestler, best known for his appearances with Extreme Championship Wrestling and World Wrestling Entertainment as D-Von Dudley. Hughes was trained by Johnny Rodz and began wrestling in 1992, competing in independent promotions in the Northeast as \"A-Train\". On April 13, 1996, at Massacre on Queens Blvd, Hughes debuted in Extreme Championship Wrestling as D-Von Dudley. His character was based on Jules Winnfield, the Bible-quoting hitman portrayed by Samuel L. Jackson in the 1994 film Pulp Fiction. Dudley feuded with the other members of the Dudley family (his kayfabe half-brothers), claiming that their comedic antics were not the way true Dudleys should act. In mid-1999, Bubba Ray and D-Von left ECW following a pay dispute and debuted in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) in September.","alterEgos":["D-Von Dudley"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1355,1418,3124,3125],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":28,"storytelling":43,"productFit":58,"riskTaking":60,"matchLayout":50,"psychology":24,"workerManagement":47,"trainingIntensity":41,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":77,"diagnosis":60,"rehabilitation":57,"prevention":46,"mediaHandling":41,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":42,"positioning":23,"reactionSpeed":27,"consistency":42,"awareness":56,"judgement":46},"picture":"D-Von Dudley.png"},{"id":114,"name":"Bully Ray","realName":"Bully Ray","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":280,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1971-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":36,"charisma":54,"micSkills":52,"condition":53,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"ability":63,"currentAbility":38,"potentialAbility":80,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Bully Ray is one of the most accomplished professional wrestlers in the history of the sport. Having captured numerous titles in both singles and tag team competition around the globe, Bully made his long-awaited IMPACT return when he shocked the world at Bound For Glory and won the Call Your Shot Gauntlet. While Bully has a reputation of stabbing his allies in the back, he has promised that this time, things will be different. With a title shot of his choosing in his possession, Bully’s odds of yet another title run in IMPACT Wrestling are promising.","alterEgos":["Bubba Ray Dudley"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1355,1418,3124,3125],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":28,"characterCoaching":82,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":63,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"Bully Ray_alt6.png"},{"id":115,"name":"Chavo Guerrero Jr.","realName":"Chavo Guerrero Jr.","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":215,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1970-10-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":30,"charisma":73,"micSkills":73,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"ability":73,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":75,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Salvador Guerrero IV also known as Chavo Guerrero and Chavo Guerrero, Jr., is a third generation American professional wrestler and member of the famed Guerrero wrestling family. He is the grandson of Gory Guerrero; the son of Chavo Guerrero, Sr.; the nephew of Eddie Guerrero, Hector Guerrero, Mando Guerrero, and Enrique Llanes; and the cousin of Javier Llanes and Hector Mejia. His grandfather, Gory Guerrero, was one of the most famous wrestlers in Mexican history. His father, Chavo Guerrero, Sr., was also a legendary wrestler in Mexico and worked in WWE as a part-time wrestler and full-time manager. One of his uncles, Eddie Guerrero, was one of WWE's biggest stars. Eddie performed for the SmackDown! brand, as did Chavo Sr. (aka Chavo Classic). Chavo Jr. has two other uncles (Mando and Hector) who have had successful careers in the business.","alterEgos":["Chavo Guerrero"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[997,3165],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":55,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":57,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":66,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"picture":"Chavo Guerrero Jr_alt3.png"},{"id":116,"name":"Chris Sabin","realName":"Chris Sabin","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":205,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1982-02-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":38,"charisma":74,"micSkills":89,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":89,"injuryProne":100,"ability":77,"currentAbility":77,"potentialAbility":79,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Whether in singles or tag team competition, Chris Sabin has been dazzling fans and winning championships all over the world for more than 15 years. He and fellow Detroit native Alex Shelley, collectively known as Motor City Machine Guns, have formed one of the top tag teams of the past decade.\r\n \r\nSabin made his ROH debut in 2003 and created an immediate buzz with his flashy in-ring style. He joined forces with Shelley in ROH in 2007. After winning championships in various promotions in the U.S. and Japan, including the prestigious IWGP Junior Heavyweight Tag Team Titles, Motor City Machine Guns finally captured the ROH World Tag Team Titles in 2017, defeating The Young Bucks at Death Before Dishonor XV.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Pinckney, Michigan, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-116","wrestlerId":116,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1234,1235,2347,2662,3690,3792,3958,4040,4041],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":72,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":77,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"picture":"Chris Sabin.png"},{"id":118,"name":"Christopher Daniels","realName":"Christopher Daniels","nickname":"","type":"trainer","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":209,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1970-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":30,"charisma":57,"micSkills":76,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"ability":61,"currentAbility":36,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"One of the “Founding Fathers” of Ring of Honor, “Almighty” Christopher Daniels has been a major player in ROH since Day One. He wrestled in the main event on the very first ROH show, The Era of Honor Begins, in 2002. A cunning ring general, as well as the self-proclaimed “Smartest Man in the Room,” Daniels reached the pinnacle of the sport when he won the ROH World Championship in 2017 after coming close on numerous occasions over the years.\r\n\r\nDaniels is also a former ROH World Television Champion and has held the ROH World Tag Team Titles with three different partners, including twice as The Addiction with longtime friend Frankie Kazarian. Toward the end of 2017, Daniels and Kazarian recruited Scorpio Sky to form the trouble-making trio SoCal Uncensored.","alterEgos":["Curryman","Suicide"],"birthplace":"Kalamazoo, Michigan, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-118","wrestlerId":118,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[941,1015,1339,1371,1446,1490,1573,1898,1899,2702],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":50,"productFit":23,"riskTaking":48,"matchLayout":41,"psychology":27,"workerManagement":24,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":57,"characterCoaching":74,"teaching":94,"diagnosis":41,"rehabilitation":51,"prevention":27,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":37,"socialMediaSavvy":34,"ruleKnowledge":48,"positioning":36,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":20,"awareness":50,"judgement":38},"picture":"Christopher Daniels_alt12.png"},{"id":120,"name":"Dixie Carter","realName":"Dixie Carter","nickname":"","type":"businessperson","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":130,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1964-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":7,"charisma":0,"micSkills":7,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":0,"injuryProne":50,"ability":0,"currentAbility":0,"potentialAbility":2,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Dixie Lee Carter-Salinas, is an American businesswoman, currently serving as president of the limited liability company TNA Entertainment. In 2002, the president of Monterey Peninsula Talent (a booking agency) contacted Carter and informed her that Total Nonstop Action Wrestling, a professional wrestling promotion, required a marketing and publicity outlet. Carter began working with TNA, but, two months later, was informed by Jeff Jarrett (a part-owner of TNA) that a key financial backer (HealthSouth Corporation, which was having financial problems due to its being investigated for accounting irregularities) had withdrawn support from TNA, and that the company was in dire straits as a result. Dixie contacted her parents, the owners of Panda Energy International, a Dallas-based energy company. In October 2002, Panda Energy purchased 71% of TNA from the HealthSouth Corporation for $250,000 USD.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":67,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":41,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":39,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":41,"characterCoaching":32,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":39,"rehabilitation":55,"prevention":32,"mediaHandling":27,"brandBuilding":37,"socialMediaSavvy":22,"ruleKnowledge":43,"positionin