American wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Japan and India. He is a 6'8\", 290lb worker who is classed as using a Brawler style. He uses the Bicycle Kick and the Inverted Full Nelson Bomb as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NJPW, NOAH, TNA, wXw, NWA, The Crash, RevPro, MLW and MLP. He is currently a The Crash Tag Team champion. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":["Festus","Luke Gallows"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-123","wrestlerId":123,"promotionId":68,"startDate":"2025-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":26200,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[971,1408,2069,2102,3922,4208,4368],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":59,"technicalCoaching":31,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":59,"consistency":64,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Luke Gallows_alt11.png","additionalContracts":[{"id":"tew-contract-123-45","wrestlerId":123,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":25600,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},{"id":"tew-contract-123-118","wrestlerId":123,"promotionId":118,"startDate":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":10500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false}],"alsoWorksFor":["MLP","NOAH"]},{"id":124,"name":"Earl Hebner","realName":"Earl Hebner","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":161,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1949-05-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1980-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":29,"charisma":71,"micSkills":92,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"ability":81,"currentAbility":37,"potentialAbility":39,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Earl William Hebner is a professional wrestling referee, and the twin brother of Dave Hebner. He is perhaps the most famous professional wrestling referee today, best known from his time as the senior referee for the World Wrestling Federation/Entertainment and later on in the same role on their Raw brand from 2002-2005. As Senior Referee, Hebner officiated most main events during his time with the company from 1988-2005. He played an extremely prominent role in the inaugural The Main Event card in 1988, in which André the Giant controversially \"defeated\" Hulk Hogan for the WWF Championship, as well as the infamous \"Montreal Screwjob\" during the main event of the 1997 Survivor Series. He also participated in an on-screen angle in mid to late 2000 where he became biased against the McMahon-Helmsley Faction for constantly and deliberately defying his authority as a referee and attacking him.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":15,"storytelling":12,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":93,"matchLayout":11,"psychology":15,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":4,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":20,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":7,"mediaHandling":20,"brandBuilding":7,"socialMediaSavvy":11,"ruleKnowledge":82,"positioning":66,"reactionSpeed":4,"consistency":2,"awareness":15,"judgement":9},"picture":"Earl Hebner_alt2.png"},{"id":125,"name":"Elijah Burke","realName":"Elijah Burke","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1978-04-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":10,"charisma":61,"micSkills":69,"condition":68,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"ability":63,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":79,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Elijah Burke is an American wrestler who works in America and Canada. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Technician Striker style. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT and NWA.","alterEgos":["D'Angelo Dinero","Da Pope"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":83,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":67,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"picture":"Elijah Burke_alt2.png"},{"id":126,"name":"Eric Bischoff","realName":"Eric Bischoff","nickname":"","type":"businessperson","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":194,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1955-05-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1987-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":39,"charisma":67,"micSkills":55,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":41,"injuryProne":50,"ability":58,"currentAbility":27,"potentialAbility":29,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Aaron Eric Bischoff is an American entrepreneur and former professional wrestling booker, producer, and on-screen personality, most known for serving as Executive Producer and later President of World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and later, the General Manager of World Wrestling Entertainment's Raw brand. With an amateur background in martial arts, Bischoff was also known to sporadically compete as an in-ring performer, and is a former WCW Hardcore Champion. Bischoff started in wrestling working for the American Wrestling Association under owner Verne Gagne and would eventually become an on-air interviewer and host until the AWA folded in 1991. In 1991, Bischoff joined World Championship Wrestling (WCW) as an announcer, debuting at The Great American Bash. In 1994, Bischoff was promoted from Executive Producer to Executive Vice President, effectively making him the boss of the entire company.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":62,"productFit":75,"riskTaking":56,"matchLayout":49,"psychology":22,"workerManagement":51,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":48,"teaching":30,"diagnosis":39,"rehabilitation":25,"prevention":41,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":22,"socialMediaSavvy":50,"ruleKnowledge":20,"positioning":60,"reactionSpeed":40,"consistency":58,"awareness":49,"judgement":30},"picture":"Eric Bischoff_alt2.png"},{"id":127,"name":"Eric Young","realName":"Eric Young","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":232,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1979-12-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":26,"charisma":62,"micSkills":61,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":90,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Eric Young, who graduated from Can-Am Wrestling School on 01 October 1998, is a Canadian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada and Japan. He is a 5'11\", 232lb worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He uses the Spiked Piledriver and the Wheelbarrow Neckbreaker as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, TNA and NXT.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Canada","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1357],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":77,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":90,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"picture":"Eric Young_alt6.png"},{"id":128,"name":"Frankie Kazarian","realName":"Frankie Kazarian","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":28,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":210,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1977-08-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":29,"charisma":66,"micSkills":89,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":100,"ability":63,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":75,"morale":"poor","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"“The Heavy Metal Rebel” Frankie Kazarian was already an accomplished veteran when he came to Ring of Honor in 2014 to join forces with longtime friend Christopher Daniels as The Addiction. Kazarian and Daniels proved to be master manipulators who sucked in ROH fans and competitors by releasing propaganda under the pseudonym “The Knights of the Rising Dawn.” Using the distraction of KRD, The Addiction captured the ROH World Tag Team Championships from ReDRagon. After losing the titles several months later, The Addiction became two-time champions when they defeated War Machine at War of the Worlds 2016.\r\n\r\nKazarian won the 2017 Honor Rumble by eliminating Jay Lethal, and toward the end of that year he and Daniels recruited Scorpio Sky to form the trouble-making trio SoCal Uncensored. Away from the ring, Kazarian plays bass guitar for the heavy metal band Vex Temper.","alterEgos":["Kaz","Kazarian","Suicide"],"birthplace":"Palm Springs, California, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-128","wrestlerId":128,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2023-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[941,1056,1371,1864,1898,2665,3296],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":69,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":62,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consi