,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hector Manuel Guerrero Lleras is a Mexican-American professional wrestler, better known simply by his paternal name, Hector Guerrero. He is a member of the famous Guerrero family, brother to the late Eddie and uncle to Chavo Jr. In 1990, Guerrero appeared in the World Wrestling Federation at the Survivor Series, performing under the name Gobbledy Gooker and wearing a turkey costume. The Gobbledy Gooker \"hatched\" from an oversized egg, which had been on display at WWF events for months prior to the Survivor Series, and was heavily hyped on television. However, crowd reaction to the gimmick was extremely negative, with fans loudly booing as the costumed Guerrero danced in the ring with announcer \"Mean\" Gene Okerlund. Rated by many as the worst gimmick in wrestling history!","alterEgos":["Gobbledy Gooker"],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":89,"storytelling":91,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":92,"psychology":89,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":34,"awareness":89,"judgement":93},"picture":"Hector Guerrero.png"},{"id":133,"name":"James Storm","realName":"James Storm","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":230,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1977-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":25,"charisma":75,"micSkills":65,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":100,"ability":72,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":85,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"James Storm is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan, Europe and Oceania. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Brawler style. He is best known for his work with IMPACT and NWA. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He was one half of the Tag Team Of The Year in 2005.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[945,1334,2001,2347],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":75,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":81,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"picture":"James Storm_alt6.png"},{"id":134,"name":"Jeff Hardy","realName":"Jeff Hardy","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":28,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":225,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1977-08-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":41000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":50,"charisma":86,"micSkills":71,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100,"ability":67,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":89,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Jeff Hardy dared the WWE Universe to dream big. Going from a scrawny teenager to one of the most popular WWE Champions in history, The Charismatic Enigma showed that anything was possible when you took a risk. \r\n\r\nWhen The Charismatic Enigma set his sights on the WWE Championship, doubts began to arise. He was unable to wrest the title away from Triple H and Randy Orton, leaving many wondering if he could reach the top of the mountain. He erased any suspicions at Armageddon 2008, when he defeated The Game and Edge in a Triple Threat Match to finally capture sports-entertainment’s richest prize.\r\n\r\nMaking a shocking return to WWE alongside his brother Matt at WrestleMania 33, he captured the Raw Tag Team Championship in a Fatal 4-Way Ladder Match and overcame Jinder Mahal during the 2018 Superstar Shake-up to lay claim to the United States Title and complete his Grand Slam.","alterEgos":["Willow The Wisp","Willow"],"birthplace":"Cameron, North Carolina, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-134","wrestlerId":134,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2024-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":41000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[164,1398,1434,1436,3454,3470],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":84,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":84,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":49,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Jeff Hardy.png"},{"id":135,"name":"Jeff Jarrett","realName":"Jeff Jarrett","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":229,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1967-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":41,"charisma":75,"micSkills":88,"condition":60,"hardcoreAbility":82,"injuryProne":100,"ability":48,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":80,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"technical","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"“Ain’t I great?” If you think Jeff Jarrett expected to hear anything other than an affirmative every time he fired that question at the WWE Universe, then you didn’t understand the character of the Fargo strutting, Technicolor dreamcoated country crooner from Music City, USA. That grinning arrogance — matched with a predilection for smashing guys over the head with a guitar — made Jarrett a career villain in both WWE and WCW. He was a successful one, too, with four reigns as WCW World Heavyweight Champion and six as WWE Intercontinental Champion with the bulk of his runs coming during a particularly excellent stretch for that title.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Hendersonville, Tennessee, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-135","wrestlerId":135,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-11-02T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1113,3015,3187],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":87,"storytelling":88,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":12,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":87,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":76,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":88,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":70,"awareness":87,"judgement":92},"picture":"Jeff Jarrett.png"},{"id":136,"name":"Jeremy Borash","realName":"Jeremy Borash","nickname":"","type":"writer","promotionId":65,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":180,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1977-05-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":9,"charisma":82,"micSkills":92,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":95,"ability":98,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":74,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"Jeremy Borash, is a former American professional wrestling play-by-play commentator, announcer, booker, producer and website designer. He was heavily involved in World Championship Wrestling, the now defunct World Wrestling All-Stars promotion, and has been a very influential staff member of Total Nonstop Action Wrestling since its inception in 2002. He is a former member of the TNA creative team and is the former host of TNA Today.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-136","wrestlerId":136,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2018-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":93,"matchLayout":52,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":18,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":7,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":24,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":18,"consistency":2,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"picture":"Jeremy Borash_alt3.png"},{"id":138,"name":"Jessie Godderz","realName":"Jessie Godderz","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1986-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":6,"charisma":63,"micSkills":64,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"ability":57,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":55,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Jessie Godderz is an American professional bodybuilder/Wrestler with the World Natural Body Building Federation from Rudd, Iowa and was a HouseGuest on Big Brother 10. In 2011, Godderz signed a contract with professional wrestling promotion Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) and was sent down to their developmental territory, Ohio Valley Wrestling for further training. On October 14, 2012, at Bound for Glory, Godderz made his TNA debut on the main roster as Tara's \"Hollywood boyfriend\". Godderz, billed simply as \"Jesse\", made his in-ring debut on the November 1 episode of Impact Wrestling, defeating ODB in an intergender match, following interference from Tara. Godderz’s goal is to inspire people who want to lose weight. He wants to be looked up to, as the figure promoting a drug-free, bodybuilding lifestyle. He states this as one of the reasons why he joined Big Brother.","alterEgos":["Jessie"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1399],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":49,"storytelling":52,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":53,"psychology":49,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":59,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":66,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":50,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":59,"consistency":68,"awareness":49,"judgement":49},"picture":"Jesse Godderz.png"},{"id":140,"name":"Kenny King","realName":"Kenny King","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":230,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1981-07-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":14,"charisma":58,"micSkills":66,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":81,"injuryProne":100,"ability":70,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":69,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kenny King has been part of a notable tag team and a faction during his career in Ring of Honor, but he has achieved his greatest success on his own. King, who made his ROH debut in 2007, scored the biggest victory of his career when he defeated New Japan Pro-Wrestling star KUSHIDA for the ROH World Television Title at Death Before Dishonor XV in 2017.\r\n\r\nBefore he began making opponents “bend the knee” in singles competition, King held the ROH World Tag Team Titles with Rhett Titus -- the duo was known as The All Night Express -- in 2012, and in 2016 he formed a faction called The Cabinet (which later became The Rebellion). In addition to his exploits in the ring, King appeared as a cast member on “The Bachelorette” in 2017.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[924],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":66,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":69,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"picture":"Kenny King_alt2.png"},{"id":141,"name":"Kurt Angle","realName":"Kurt Angle","nickname":"","type":"scout","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1968-12-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":58,"charisma":90,"micSkills":91,"condition":51,"hardcoreAbility":93,"injuryProne":90,"ability":98,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kurt Angle’s intensity was unmatched, and his technical wrestling skills were unparalleled. Possessing an unprecedented competitive streak that fueled him to become a 1996 Olympic Gold Medalist, Angle dominated the amateur ranks before emerging as one of the most successful WWE Superstars of all time.\r\n\r\nStarting his athletic career as a football and wrestling star in his hometown of Pittsburgh, he soon became one of the top amateur wrestlers in the U.S., winning a pair of NCAA titles at Clarion University. But Angle truly captured national attention in 1996 when he won the 220-pound freestyle wrestling competition at the Olympic Games in Atlanta with a broken neck.\r\n\r\n","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1151],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":49,"storytelling":24,"productFit":31,"riskTaking":57,"matchLayout":41,"psychology":21,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":21,"technicalCoaching":25,"characterCoaching":31,"teaching":45,"diagnosis":55,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":29,"ruleKnowledge":27,"positioning":52,"reactionSpeed":43,"consistency":48,"awareness":22,"judgement":97},"picture":"Kurt Angle_alt6.png"},{"id":142,"name":"Victoria","realName":"Victoria","nickname":"","type":"trainer","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":155,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1971-02-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":21,"charisma":87,"micSkills":94,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":91,"injuryProne":96,"ability":79,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Victoria was not a lady to mess with. A two-time Women’s Champion who stomped icons like Trish Stratus and Lita in brutal Hardcore Matches, the powerful beauty broke ground in the women's division and left a trail of woe behind her.\r\n\r\nVictoria debuted in July 2002 as an eager competitor against reigning Women’s Champion Trish Stratus on Sunday Night Heat, but the loss proved her much more demented. Victoria continued to target Stratus, claiming the champion double-crossed her during their respective fitness model days.\r\n\r\nHer twisted mind games and sneak attacks grew worse into the fall, baiting Stratus into a Women’s Championship Hardcore Match at Survivor Series 2002. The raven-haired Diva brutalized Stratus in Madison Square Garden with chairs and a garbage can before finishing the champ off with a suplex to claim her first Women’s Title.","alterEgos":["Tara","Lisa Marie Varon"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":44,"storytelling":57,"productFit":22,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":24,"workerManagement":36,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":74,"teaching":71,"diagnosis":23,"rehabilitation":32,"prevention":30,"mediaHandling":36,"brandBuilding":22,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":39,"positioning":26,"reactionSpeed":48,"consistency":51,"awareness":39,"judgement":55},"picture":"Tara.png"},{"id":143,"name":"Mark Haskins","realName":"Mark Haskins","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":185,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1988-06-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-07-22T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":9,"charisma":71,"micSkills":55,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"ability":61,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":71,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Mark Haskins is an English wrestler who works in the British Isles and Europe. He is a 5'7\", 185lb worker who is classed as using a Technician Striker style. He uses the Sharpshooter as his finisher. He is best known for his work with TNA, Dragon Gate, PWG, ROH, wXw, RevPro, PROGRESS, AAW, OTT, FCP, Smash, Defiant, ICW and SWE. He is married to Vicky Haskins.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"England","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[449,1975,2308],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":61,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":70,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Mark Haskins_alt3.png"},{"id":144,"name":"Matt Morgan","realName":"Matt Morgan","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":300,"height":210,"dateOfBirth":"1976-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":15,"charisma":87,"micSkills":69,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"ability":55,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":85,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Matt Morgan was an American wrestler who has since left the business. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, AJPW and IMPACT. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1233,3237],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":64,"productFit":60,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":74,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":74,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":65,"awareness":59,"judgement":59},"picture":"Matt Morgan_alt2.png"},{"id":145,"name":"Mickie James","realName":"Mickie James","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":124,"height":160,"dateOfBirth":"1979-08-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":35,"charisma":73,"micSkills":78,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":100,"ability":56,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":75,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Throughout much of Mickie James’ WWE career, there are some who considered her a peppy, energetic sweetheart. But she’s proven to be as dangerous in the ring as any that came before her.\r\n\r\nA lifelong Virginian, Mickie spent years honing her craft with the goal of becoming one of the greatest female Superstars in history. To this end, the athletic master of a ring-pounding Implant DDT has gone to war with the likes of Trish Stratus, Lita, Maryse, Gail Kim and Alicia Fox. She fought in legendary battles against Beth Phoenix and against simply “flawless” adversaries Team LayCool, Michelle McCool and Layla. And she did it all while amassing WWE gold and all the glory that came with it.\r\n\r\nMickie has captured six Women’s Championships, and at one point, became the second Superstar to hold both the Women’s and the Divas Titles simultaneously. She did this all while establishing herself as one of the alpha females of WWE.","alterEgos":["Alexis Laree"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1546],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":78,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":82,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"picture":"Mickie James_alt13.png"},{"id":146,"name":"Mike Knox","realName":"Mike Knox","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":79,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":293,"height":195,"dateOfBirth":"1978-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":24600,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":7,"charisma":51,"micSkills":48,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"ability":55,"currentAbility":41,"potentialAbility":43,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Mike Knox is an American wrestler who works in America and Canada. He is a Heavyweight who is classed as using a Powerhouse style. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT and NWA.","alterEgos":["Knux"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-146","wrestlerId":146,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2021-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":24600,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3831],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":47,"storytelling":50,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":51,"psychology":47,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":24,"characterCoaching":50,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":68,"awareness":47,"judgement":68},"picture":"Mike Knox_alt5.png"},{"id":147,"name":"Mike Tenay","realName":"Mike Tenay","nickname":"","type":"commentator","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":180,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1956-02-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":18,"charisma":0,"micSkills":9,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":0,"injuryProne":24,"ability":15,"currentAbility":7,"potentialAbility":9,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Mike Tenay is a professional wrestling play-by-play announcer. He is best known for his time working with World Championship Wrestling and Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. Mike Tenay made his WCW announcing debut during the WCW-co-promoted AAA When Worlds Collide pay-per-view in November 1994. He is considered one of the foremost wrestling historians which earned him the nickname \"The Professor.\" Current TNA Executive Producer and former WCW president Eric Bischoff has described Tenay as \"a walking encyclopedia of knowledge.\" In early 2002, Tenay was approached by Jeff Jarrett regarding the play-by-play announcer's slot with Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. Tenay became the voice of the upstart company when it launched in June 2002.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":40,"storytelling":36,"productFit":57,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":34,"psychology":44,"workerManagement":20,"trainingIntensity":30,"technicalCoaching":41,"characterCoaching":38,"teaching":56,"diagnosis":41,"rehabilitation":57,"prevention":36,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":92,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":54,"positioning":41,"reactionSpeed":26,"consistency":29,"awareness":44,"judgement":26},"picture":"Mike Tenay.png"},{"id":148,"name":"Mr. Anderson","realName":"Ken Anderson","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":195,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1976-03-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":27,"charisma":78,"micSkills":75,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":87,"ability":52,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":84,"morale":"poor","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kenneth C. Anderson is an American professional wrestler and actor better known by his ring name Mr. Kennedy. After signing with WWE, Anderson made his debut on the SmackDown! roster as Ken Kennedy in August 2005. In September 2006 he captured his first title with the company, the WWE United States Championship, and would hold onto it for a month. The following year, at WrestleMania 23, Anderson won the annual Money in the Bank ladder match, a contract, which guarantees a match for any of WWE's three top titles. He was released from his WWE contract on May 29, 2009. In January 2010 Anderson signed a one-year deal with Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. He would make his return to the company at the Genesis pay-per-view on January 17, 2010, working under the ring name Mr. Anderson.","alterEgos":["Mr. Kennedy"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":82,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":61,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"picture":"Ken Anderson_alt3.png"},{"id":149,"name":"Nick Aldis","realName":"Nick Aldis","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":242,"height":190,"dateOfBirth":"1986-11-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":38,"charisma":84,"micSkills":83,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":100,"ability":76,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":80,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Nick Aldis is an English wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan, Europe and India. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is one half of British Invasion alongside Doug Williams. He is best known for his work with AAA, NOAH, IMPACT, ROH, NWA, CWFH and CZW. He is married to Mickie James.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Docking, Norfolk, England","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-149","wrestlerId":149,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2023-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[965,2816,2822,3368,3369],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":84,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Nick Aldis.png"},{"id":150,"name":"ODB","realName":"ODB","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":130,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1978-06-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":15,"charisma":55,"micSkills":62,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":36,"injuryProne":100,"ability":55,"currentAbility":41,"potentialAbility":63,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Jessica Kresa is an American professional wrestler better known as ODB (short for One Dirty Bitch). Kresa's athletic background is in ice hockey, which her father encouraged her to pursue. She began watching professional wrestling as a child. She enjoyed watching wrestlers such as The Killer Bees. Kresa got her start when she tried out for the first season of the World Wrestling Federation's reality show, WWF Tough Enough. She made the top 25, but missed the final cut for the show. On June 5, 2006, Kresa debuted in Ohio Valley Wrestling as a villain under the ring name ODB. Kresa was contacted by Total Nonstop Action Wrestling to appear at their annual pay-per-view Bound for Glory. She made her in-ring re-debut at Bound for Glory, participating in a 10 Knockout Gauntlet to crown the first-ever Knockout Champion.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":78,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":67,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"ODB_alt5.png"},{"id":152,"name":"Gunner","realName":"Gunner","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":244,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1982-06-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":14,"charisma":54,"micSkills":34,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":40,"injuryProne":100,"ability":47,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":39,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Chad Lail is an American professional wrestler better known by the ring name Gunner. In TNA, Lail was a member of the Immortal stable and a former one-time TNA Television Champion. In addition to wrestling for TNA, Lail also performs for various promotions on the independent circuit under the ring name Phill Shatter. After serving in the Iraq War, Phill Shatter signed with NWA Anarchy along with fellow Iraq War veteran Truitt Fields. Shatter appeared at Ring of Honor's The Big Bang! pay-per-view on April 3, 2010. At the June 23, 2010, tapings of TNA's Impact! television show, Shatter made his TNA debut, along with Mikael Judas, as TNA's on-air security. On the July 29, 2010 edition of TNA Impact! taping, Shatter, now using the name Gunner and Mikael Judas, using the name Murphy, came out after an altercation involving Jeff Hardy and Mr. Anderson with Matt Morgan, and attacked Hardy and Anderson.","alterEgos":["Phill Shatter","Jaxson Ryker"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1334,2337,2755],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":46,"storytelling":49,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":50,"psychology":46,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":45,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":61,"awareness":46,"judgement":68},"picture":"Gunner.png"},{"id":153,"name":"Mr. Stone","realName":"Robbie E","nickname":"","type":"commentator","promotionId":65,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":201,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1983-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":19,"charisma":21,"micSkills":28,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":100,"ability":39,"currentAbility":33,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"Rob Eckos is an American wrestler who works in America and Canada. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is best known for his work with NXT, IMPACT, NOAH and GCW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":["Robbie E","Robert Stone"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-153","wrestlerId":153,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2019-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1399,2818],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":70,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":71,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"picture":"Rob Eckos_alt.png"},{"id":155,"name":"Rob Van Dam","realName":"Rob Van Dam","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":235,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1970-12-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":38,"charisma":68,"micSkills":86,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":89,"injuryProne":100,"ability":54,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":86,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Who has two thumbs, scored a historic WWE Championship win in New York City and is perhaps the most popular ECW icon of all time? Say it with him now: “Rob! Van! Dam!”\r\n\r\nWhen the chilled out martial artist from Battle Creek, Mich. broke into ECW in 1996, he made an impact like few grapplers ever have. Trained alongside future partner and rival Sabu by Sabu’s uncle, The Original Sheik, RVD had the sound fundamentals needed to thrive in the Land of Extreme. Van Dam’s laidback demeanor directly contradicted his agility in the squared circle, which made him an instant favorite among the Philadelphia faithful. He quickly scored victories over Axl Rotten, Mikey Whipwreck and Sabu, but it was his partnership with the latter that launched The Whole Dam Show to a new level.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1130,1303,1304,3281,3282,3283],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":78,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":68,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Rob Van Dam_alt5.png"},{"id":156,"name":"Robert Roode","realName":"Bobby Roode","nickname":"","type":"writer","promotionId":64,"base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":235,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1976-05-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":37,"charisma":75,"micSkills":83,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"ability":91,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Wherever Robert Roode goes, he makes sure everyone knows of his “glorious” ambitions.\r\n\r\nAlready a world-renowned Superstar by the time he joined NXT in July 2016, Roode promised from the beginning to bring the brand to new heights. He backed up his talk when he defeated Shinsuke Nakamura at TakeOver: San Antonio to win the NXT Championship, beginning an eight-month reign.\r\n\r\nHaving reached the peak of NXT, Roode turned his sights on WWE's main roster. Roode signed with SmackDown LIVE in the hopes of making Team Blue a little more glorious and immediately started a rivalry with Dolph Ziggler before capturing the vacant United States Championship in a tournament. Then, in the 2018 Superstar Shake-up, Roode came to Raw and won the Raw Tag Team Titles alongside Chad Gable.","alterEgos":["Bobby Roode"],"birthplace":"Peterborough, Ontario, Canada","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-156","wrestlerId":156,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[945,1026,1357,1845,1965],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":11,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":73,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":89,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":80,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"picture":"Bobby Roode_alt13.png"},{"id":157,"name":"Samoa Joe","realName":"Samoa Joe","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":279,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1979-03-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":50,"charisma":88,"micSkills":100,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":96,"ability":80,"currentAbility":80,"potentialAbility":92,"morale":"good","presentation":"heel","prestige":"mid","style":"submission","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"A world-traveled veteran of the mat game, the 282-pound Samoa Joe has used a blistering, MMA-inspired offense to rack up championships in top promotions across the globe. Before he ever set foot in WWE, Samoa Joe had already thrown down with the likes of John Cena, Daniel Bryan, Seth Rollins and Cesaro throughout his storied career.\r\n\r\nStill, despite his pedigree, the thought of Samoa Joe entering a WWE ring seemed to be relegated to the imaginations of fantasy matchmakers worldwide. Yet, after barreling through WWE NXT and twice capturing the NXT Title, Joe officially signed to Monday Night Raw in 2017 and has since unleashed his vicious squared circle philosophy on Raw and SmackDown LIVE against opponents like AJ Styles, Roman Reigns, and even Brock Lesnar.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Orange County, California, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-157","wrestlerId":157,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[113,1015,2822,3644],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":80,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":65,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"picture":"Samoa Joe.png"},{"id":158,"name":"Shawn Hernandez","realName":"Shawn Hernandez","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":285,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1973-02-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":12,"charisma":66,"micSkills":51,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":42,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Shawn Hernandez is an American wrestler who works exclusively in North America. He is a Heavyweight who is classed as using a Brawler style. He is best known for his work with AAA, IMPACT, NWA, AJPW, ROH, MLW, IWRG, ZERO1, Lucha Ungrnd and IWA-MS. He was one half of the Tag Team Of The Year in 2006.","alterEgos":["Hernandez"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[997,1152,1233],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":41,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":36,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":59,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":79,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"picture":"Shawn Hernandez_alt.png"},{"id":159,"name":"Joaquin Wilde","realName":"DJ Z","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":169,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1986-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":26,"charisma":74,"micSkills":69,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"ability":63,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":67,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Joaquin Wilde used to literally light up the room when he made his entrance, at least until he turned to the dark side and Legado del Fantasma.\r\n\r\nAlthough Wilde’s talent is undeniable, that doesn’t mean his path to NXT was always a sure bet. While wrestling in Mexico in 2017, two years before inking a contract with NXT, Wilde suffered a ruptured colon and internal bleeding during a match. The injury threatened to not only end his career just as it was reaching full bloom, but his life. Miraculously, he pulled through, and being the fighter that he is, Wilde returned from the setback stronger than before.\r\n\r\nWilde’s resilience isn’t surprising, considering his upbringing. Raised by a single mother who emigrated from the Philippines, Wilde witnessed firsthand what it means to make sacrifices and overcome hardship.\r\n\r\n","alterEgos":["DJ Z","Shiima Xion","Zema Ion"],"birthplace":"Los Angeles, California, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-159","wrestlerId":159,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2019-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1755,2161],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":68,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"Joaquin Wilde.png"},{"id":160,"name":"SoCal Val","realName":"SoCal Val","nickname":"","type":"commentator","promotionId":44,"base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":114,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1986-03-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":10500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":6,"charisma":24,"micSkills":23,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":32,"injuryProne":96,"ability":30,"currentAbility":27,"potentialAbility":31,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"SoCal Val is an American woman who works as a colour commentator, a manager and an on-screen personality. She is best known for her work with IMPACT and SHINE.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-160","wrestlerId":160,"promotionId":44,"startDate":"2022-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23