stling. Jordan uses his wits along with his never stop, never-quit, never-say-die attitude to top his opponents in the squared circle. While here at NXT, Jason Jordan has gained tons of experience and is constantly building an arsenal of attacks.","alterEgos":["Nathan Everhart"],"birthplace":"Tinley Park, Illinois, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-197","wrestlerId":197,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[927,928,2745],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":59,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":69,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"picture":"Jason Jordan_alt5.png"},{"id":199,"name":"Joel Redman","realName":"Joel Redman","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":218,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1987-02-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":64,"micSkills":66,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"ability":42,"currentAbility":38,"potentialAbility":42,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Joel Redman is an English wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Technician style. He is best known for his work with NXT, wXw, AJPW and RevPro.","alterEgos":["Oliver Grey"],"birthplace":"England","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[459,964],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":46,"storytelling":52,"productFit":60,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":54,"psychology":46,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":40,"characterCoaching":56,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":68,"awareness":46,"judgement":52},"picture":"Oliver Grey.png"},{"id":200,"name":"Joey Mercury","realName":"Joey Mercury","nickname":"","type":"trainer","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":207,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1979-07-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":8,"charisma":69,"micSkills":75,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":100,"ability":93,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":72,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Flashy, arrogant and overconfident, Joey Mercury and his tag partner, Johnny Nitro, looked like the typical brash upstarts who would quickly be put in their place when they debuted on SmackDown in April 2005. Instead, they defeated Rey Mysterio & Eddie Guerrero to win the WWE Tag Team Championships in their very first match.\r\n\r\nStill, despite his three championship victories, Mercury's most memorable moment came during a losing effort. At Armageddon in 2006, MNM clashed with Paul London & Brian Kendrick, William Regal & Dave Taylor and The Hardys in a brutal Fatal 4-Way Ladder Match for the WWE Tag Team Titles. Devastating from the start, the bout took its toll on every competitor involved, but Mercury got the worst of it when he was blasted directly in the face with a ladder. The impact was so intense that it shattered the competitor's nose and caused him to be pulled from the ring and rushed directly to the emergency room.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1226,2756],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":45,"storytelling":33,"productFit":42,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":47,"workerManagement":54,"trainingIntensity":83,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":71,"teaching":79,"diagnosis":31,"rehabilitation":39,"prevention":33,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":43,"positioning":38,"reactionSpeed":31,"consistency":39,"awareness":38,"judgement":22},"picture":"Joey Mercury.png"},{"id":201,"name":"Juice Robinson","realName":"Juice Robinson","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1989-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":36,"charisma":67,"micSkills":86,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"ability":72,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":87,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Juice Robinson is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, AEW, CMLL, IMPACT, NOAH, NXT, NJoA, ROH, RevPro, AAW, OTT, IWA-MS and CZW. He is engaged to Toni Storm.","alterEgos":["CJ Parker"],"birthplace":"Joliet, Illinois, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-201","wrestlerId":201,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1812,2360,2591],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":80,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":68,"awareness":61,"judgement":77},"picture":"Juice Robinson.png"},{"id":202,"name":"KAZMA SAKAMOTO","realName":"KAZMA SAKAMOTO","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":231,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1982-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":7,"charisma":46,"micSkills":48,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":57,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"KAZMA SAKAMOTO is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NOAH, AJPW, Dragongate, GLEAT and WRESTLE-1.","alterEgos":["KAZMA","Sakamoto"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3096,4336],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":66,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":74,"awareness":61,"judgement":77},"picture":"KAZMA SAKAMOTO.png"},{"id":203,"name":"Martin Stone","realName":"Martin Stone","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":190,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1981-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":18,"charisma":66,"micSkills":73,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":82,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":65,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"From smashmouth strikes to classically applied wrestling holds, Danny Burch embodies many of British wrestling’s most enduring traits. The East Ender’s ring generalship comes from more than 14 years of transatlantic competition, starting with his schooling under English masters Tony & Dino Scarlo. Burch has been knocking out teeth in NXT dating back to 2012, and in January 2017, he notched a new milestone as a competitor in the WWE U.K. Championship Tournament. However, it was The Guv’nor’s sensational series of matches against likeminded toughie Oney Lorcan that summer that opened new doors for the rugged Londoner.","alterEgos":["Danny Burch"],"birthplace":"England","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[432,459,1685,2812],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":49,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":68,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"picture":"Danny Burch.png"},{"id":205,"name":"Matthew Rehwoldt","realName":"Matt Rehwoldt","nickname":"","type":"commentator","promotionId":28,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":216,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1987-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":14,"charisma":43,"micSkills":61,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"ability":58,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":57,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Matt Rehwoldt is a retired American wrestler who works primarily as a colour commentator. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT, NXT and NJoA. He is married to Shaul Guerrero.","alterEgos":["Matt Rehwoldt","Aiden English","Matt Morris"],"birthplace":"Chicago, Illinois, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-205","wrestlerId":205,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2021-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1522,1554,2676,3791],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":74,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":62,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"picture":"Matthew Rehwoldt.png"},{"id":206,"name":"Tyler Breeze","realName":"Breeze","nickname":"","type":"trainer","promotionId":65,"base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":204,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1988-01-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":23,"charisma":75,"micSkills":91,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"ability":87,"currentAbility":80,"potentialAbility":85,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"A deadly fighter in the vein of similarly stunning greats like “Ravishing” Rick Rude, Breeze never misses an opportunity to apply his pristine craft and leave his opponents black and blue in the process. He was an institution during the formative years of WWE NXT, orbiting but never landing the NXT Championship as he took on the likes of Sami Zayn, Finn Bálor, and even international legend Jushin “Thunder” Liger.\r\n\r\nNot that he let any of his losses get him down. Like any social climber looking for the next big thing, Breeze is constantly focused on tackling new challenges, such as teaming with fellow sartorial slueth Fandango as The Fashion Police on SmackDown and issuing citations to anyone who committed a fashion faux pas. That duo stole the hearts of the WWE Universe with their weekly \"Fashion Files\" show, and they achieved their greatest victory by defeating Imperium to become NXT Tag Team Champions.","alterEgos":["Breeze","Mattias Wild"],"birthplace":"Penticton, British Columbia, Canada","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDat