s one half of The World Class Tag Team alongside Gedo. He is best known for his work with NJPW.","alterEgos":["Captain NOAH"],"birthplace":"Minato, Tokyo, Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-345","wrestlerId":345,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1071,1567],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":47,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Jado.png"},{"id":346,"name":"Masato Tanaka","realName":"Masato Tanaka","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":208,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1973-02-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-07-23T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":27,"charisma":65,"micSkills":74,"condition":59,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"ability":74,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":80,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Masato Tanaka is a Japanese professional wrestler, best known for his appearances with Frontier Martial Arts Wrestling in Japan and in Extreme Championship Wrestling in the United States. He is currently working in Pro Wrestling ZERO1. Also makes alot of appearances for New Japan Pro Wrestling. Tanaka trained under Atsushi Onita, and debuted on July 23, 1993 in Saga City, facing Ricky Fuji. He quickly began working for FMW, widely regarded as the most hardcore professional wrestling promotion in Japan. ECW owner Paul Heyman became interested in Tanaka, and eventually hired him. Tanaka debuted in ECW on March 1, 1998 at Living Dangerously, defeating Doug Furnas. In July 1998 he reprised his feud with Awesome, who he defeated at Heat Wave 1998. Tanaka returned to FMW in 2000. On November 15, 2012, Tanaka entered a tournament to determine the inaugural NEVER Openweight Champion.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[623,1004,1013,2305,3059],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":56,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":62,"socialMediaSavvy":37,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":65,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"picture":"Masato Tanaka_alt1.png"},{"id":347,"name":"Yujiro Takahashi","realName":"Yujiro Takahashi","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":38,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":209,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1981-01-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":11,"charisma":70,"micSkills":51,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":52,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yujiro Takahashi, a 2004 graduate of the New Japan Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America