n Utah, American Xtreme in Utah, Real Mexican Wrestling in Utah and Future Stars Of Wrestling in Las Vegas.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":27,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":27,"brandBuilding":5,"socialMediaSavvy":12,"ruleKnowledge":47,"positioning":38,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Jeremy Hardy.png"},{"id":968,"name":"Latin Lover","realName":"Latin Lover","nickname":"","type":"writer","promotionId":5,"base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":216,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1967-10-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":6,"charisma":89,"micSkills":83,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":81,"injuryProne":100,"ability":90,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":50,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Victor Manuel Resendiz Ruiz is a Mexican Luchador  and actor. He is best known under his ring name Latin Lover, which he is also credited as for his acting career. Resendiz is best known for wrestling in the Mexican Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) promotion, but has also worked for the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) and currently works for the Perros del Mal and Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) promotions under the ring name Latino. Resendiz and his partner Mariana Vallejo Isrrade won the very first Bailando por un Sueño dance competition in 2005.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-968","wrestlerId":968,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2024-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3181],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":70,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":71,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"picture":"Latin Lover.png"},{"id":977,"name":"Angel Blue","realName":"Angel Blue","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":108,"height":152,"dateOfBirth":"1990-08-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":0,"charisma":27,"micSkills":55,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":38,"injuryProne":100,"ability":36,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":40,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Angel Blue was trained by both Lance Hoyt and Wally Darkmon before making her debut in PCW on their Uncut shows, originally as Alektra Blue(not to be confused with the adult film star of the same name). She has since been working on the Texas independent circuit as \"The Mega Star\" Angel Blue. Blue has made her biggest splash in ACW in Austin. Her first run in ACW saw her as a member of the Smurf Nation and winning the ACW Joshi Title. Her latest run has seen her align herself with the promotion's owner, Darin Childs, on a mission to reclaim what she believes is her rightful ACW Joshi Title.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":44,"productFit":40,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":46,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":40,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":39,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":39,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":8,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":53,"awareness":38,"judgement":39},"picture":"Angel Blue.png"},{"id":983,"name":"JD Griffey","realName":"JD Griffey","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":205,"height":190,"dateOfBirth":"1984-05-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":1,"charisma":38,"micSkills":56,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"ability":47,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":43,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"\"Flawless\" Jerome Daniels has been flawless LONG before two bimbos claimed to be flawless(even though they were anything but). Jerome began his career in PCW(Texas), and would venture his way over to XCW, where he joined up with manager Lance Romance and his stable, International Playaz Club. He then went on to team with Nobe Bryant to win the NWA Texas Tag Team Titles on two occasions. Lately, he's been teaming with \"Main Event\" Mike Foxx and Byron Wilcott as Team ATM. The trio would utilize the Freebird Rule as they won the NWA TXO Tag Team Titles. In other promotions, Jerome and Byron team up under the tag team name of \"Addictive and Expensive.\"","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":57,"productFit":61,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":61,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":64,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":66,"awareness":53,"judgement":56},"picture":"Jerome Daniels.png"},{"id":997,"name":"Ric Manning","realName":"Ric Manning","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":229,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1957-06-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1977-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":1,"charisma":64,"micSkills":86,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"ability":69,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":34,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Ric Manning has probably worked for almost every Texas wrestling show under the sun, including NWA Southwest, PCW(Arlington), XCW, NTWA... the list goes on and on. A class act who stays out of backstage squabbles, politics and the like, and manages to get along with everybody. No one seems to have a bad thing to say about the Texas based referee who was trained by David Manning of WCCW fame. While refereeing in XCW, he refereed under the pseudonym of \"George Lucas,\" a nickname he earned for bearing a resemblance to the movie director of the same name. Ric also appeared on \"Walker: Texas Ranger\" with Rowdy Roddy Piper and Rugged Rod Price in an episode filmed at the famed Dallas Sportatorium.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":48,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":41,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":50,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":73,"positioning":58,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":83,"awareness":68,"judgement":41},"picture":"Rick Manning.png"},{"id":998,"name":"Rob Moore","realName":"Rob Moore","nickname":"","type":"commentator","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":282,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1961-09-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1981-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":1,"charisma":42,"micSkills":53,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":30,"potentialAbility":32,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Despite having never worked for any of the bigger companies, Rob Moore is a very capable announcer, and is very professional, staying out of any backstage politics and strife, managing to get along with everybody. Texas promotions he has called play by play for include NWA Southwest, PCW in Arlington, XCW in Denton, and most recently, IHWE and Killer Tim Brooks' NTWA.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":70,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Rob Moore.png"},{"id":1000,"name":"Ryan Davidson","realName":"Ryan Davidson","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":242,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1985-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":1,"charisma":68,"micSkills":59,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"ability":69,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":63,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"\"Ruthless\" Ryan Davidson is an Oklahoma based wrestler that works shows mostly in Oklahoma and Texas. He had worked for Total Texas Wrestling in Graham, Texas, as well as for Texas All-Star Wrestling. He received further training and really honed his skills for Booker T's PWA in Houston, Texas, where he is a former Iron Man and Tag Team Champion. Ryan made an appearance on WWE Monday Night Raw in January 2007, portraying a security guard that was confiscating DX signs, and ranked #18 in the 2005 Oklafan Top 50, and shot up to #2 on the Oklafan Top 50 the following year. He also clocked in at #60 on the 2007 Indywarz Texas Top 100.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":62,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":72,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Ryan Davidson.png"},{"id":1002,"name":"Baron Von Storm","realName":"Tim Storm","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":79,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":260,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1965-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":24600,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":6,"charisma":56,"micSkills":67,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"ability":50,"currentAbility":25,"potentialAbility":27,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Tim Storm is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Light Heavyweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with NWA and CWFH. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":["Tim Storm"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1002","wrestlerId":1002,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2016-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":24600,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3019,3964],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":28,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":69,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"picture":"Tim Storm.png"},{"id":1006,"name":"El Oriental","realName":"El Oriental","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1972-12-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":7,"charisma":62,"micSkills":75,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"ability":59,"currentAbility":37,"potentialAbility":39,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Noé Astro Moreno León is a Mexican Luchador known under the ring name El Oriental. He is the son of wrestler and promoter Alfonso \"Acorazado\" Moreno and has worked over 70 tours of Japan. The person who would later become known as El Oriental was born on December 6, 1972 son of Mexican luchador and wrestling promoter Alfonso Moreno. Later on Moreno along with Dr. Wagner and Blue Panther trained El Oriental for his professional wrestling career. He made his debut on October 23, 1992 in Arena Azteca Budokan, the arena his father operated at the time. El Oriental adopted the ring name upon making his debut and has competed exclusively under that name since then. Early in his career he worked mainly in or around his home state of Ciudad Nezahualcóyotl, Mexico State, often working with his sisters Cynthia, Rossy and Esther Moreno.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3136,3167],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":78,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"picture":"El Oriental_alt.png"},{"id":1007,"name":"Esther Moreno","realName":"Esther Moreno","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"F","weight":130,"height":149,"dateOfBirth":"1969-02-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":66,"micSkills":59,"condition":59,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":93,"ability":49,"currentAbility":28,"potentialAbility":28,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"María Esther Moreno León is a Mexican luchadora, best known under the ring name Esther Moreno. In AAA she is a former 2 time AAA Reina de Reinas Champion. In the early 1990s Esther and her sister Cynthia Moreno travelled to Japan to wrestle for All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling. On April 21, 1991 the Moreno sisters defeated Etsuko Mita and Mima Shimoda to win the AJW Tag Team Championship, making them the first Mexican team to hold a championship in Japan.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3137,3138,3139],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":47,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":58,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":47,"consistency":47,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Esther Moreno.png"},{"id":1008,"name":"Shinjiro Otani","realName":"Shinjiro Otani","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":45,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":214,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1972-07-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":13,"charisma":67,"micSkills":80,"condition":1,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"ability":77,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Shinjiro Otani is a Japanese professional wrestler contracted to Pro Wrestling ZERO1. Otani is also the acting President of the company. Otani was the first WCW World Cruiserweight Champion, defeating Wild Pegasus in a tournament final to be crowned champion on March 20, 1996. This was the start of his push as a legitimate junior heavyweight contender. Over the years, Otani earned the J-Crown and was also part of the first IWGP Junior Heavyweight Tag Team Champions with Tatsuhito Takaiwa. On January 4, 2013, at Wrestle Kingdom 7 in Tokyo Dome, Otani made a special return to New Japan, when he replaced an injured Daichi Hashimoto in a tag team match, where he and Keiji Mutoh were defeated by Hiroyoshi Tenzan and Satoshi Kojima.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2028-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1008","wrestlerId":1008,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[623,2317,2954,2955,2956,3059,3224,3225],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":79,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":79,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":66,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":62,"awareness":79,"judgement":87},"picture":"Shinjiro Otani.png"},{"id":1009,"name":"Johnny Gargano","realName":"Johnny Gargano","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":198,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1987-08-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":40,"charisma":87,"micSkills":100,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":100,"ability":84,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":88,"morale":"fair","presentation":"heel","prestige":"mid","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Since starting his path to Superstardom, the man known as Johnny Wrestling has heard “no” more times than he can count. When he first broke in, he was told he was too small to be a serious contender, and he still has the rejection email he received after attending a WWE tryout in 2015, keeping it as a reminder of how far he’s come. Because make no mistake, the self-described “chubby kid from Cleveland” — who used to play-wrestle on mattresses and aspire to become the next Shawn Michaels — has come a long, long way. Starting out as an unsigned free agent, Gargano first made his mark in NXT in a tag team with Tommaso Ciampa. The duo known as #DIY lifted NXT’s tandem division to new heights, producing classic rivalries against the likes of The Revival and AOP, as well as an impressive NXT Tag Team Title reign. After the team’s implosion in 2017, a fate brought on by Ciampa’s ruthless betrayal of Gargano, the two Superstars experienced more ups and downs than a rollercoaster ride.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Lakewood, Ohio, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1009","wrestlerId":1009,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[906,1352,2454,2809,3856],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":81,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"picture":"Johnny Gargano.png"},{"id":1010,"name":"CIMA","realName":"CIMA","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":180,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1977-11-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":17,"charisma":56,"micSkills":80,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":74,"injuryProne":100,"ability":74,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":66,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"CIMA is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with WCW, NJPW, CMLL, AEW, AJPW, Dragongate, PWG, wXw, DDT, ROH, MLW, BJW, ZERO1, GLEAT, The Crash, WRESTLE-1, DEFY, IWRG, FCP, DTU and SWE. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1266,1327,1555,2006,2297],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":83,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":64,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"picture":"CIMA_alt1.png"},{"id":1011,"name":"Stalker Ichikawa","realName":"Stalker Ichikawa","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":143,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1974-10-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":66,"micSkills":48,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":36,"injuryProne":100,"ability":49,"currentAbility":33,"potentialAbility":33,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"comedy","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"counter","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kanji Ichikawa better known by his stage name \"Hollywood\" Stalker Ichikawa is a Japanese professional wrestler. Stalker Ichikawa is one of the most popular superstars from Dragon Gate. A member of Último Dragón's Toryumon Dojo second class gifted with an extensive amateur wrestling background, Ichikawa is one of the many comedy characters whose purpose is more based on entertaining the fans than it is to actually win matches. Stalker's matches do not last very long, often within five to ten minutes tops. His offenses would have little to no effect on his opponents and they would simply side-step whenever he attempts any sort of high flying move. In some cases, just as Stalker is about to be hit by his opponent's finisher some one, usually his wife Namiko, would throw in the towel to stop the match. The opponent would still hit him with his finisher shortly after.","alterEgos":["Jushin Thunder Ichikawa","Kono Mama Ichikawa"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":82,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":20,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":65,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"picture":"Stalker Ichikawa.png"},{"id":1012,"name":"Shingo Takagi","realName":"Shingo Takagi","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":38,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1982-11-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":35,"charisma":97,"micSkills":75,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":91,"injuryProne":100,"ability":74,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":86,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Shingo Takagi, a 2004 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, Dragongate, wXw and ROH. He is currently the NJPW King Of Pro Wrestling champion. He was voted Young Wrestler Of The Year in 2005.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Tatomi, Nakakoma District (now Chūō), Yamanashi, Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1012","wrestlerId":1012,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2018-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1229,1351,1785,2944,2949,4293],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":46,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":84,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"picture":"Shingo Takagi.png"},{"id":1017,"name":"Nobuhiko Takada","realName":"Nobuhiko Takada","nickname":"","type":"manager","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1962-04-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1981-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":7,"charisma":68,"micSkills":65,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":90,"ability":67,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":32,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Nobuhiko Takada is a Japanese mixed martial arts fighter and professional wrestler. He is best known for helping to popularize shoot-style professional wrestling, as one of the biggest stars of the UWF in the '80s and '90s. Despite his irregular fight record and kayfabe politics, Takada is credited with the existence of PRIDE and the Japanese MMA boom, and is widely considered to be one of the main promotors of mixed martial arts both nationally and internationally. Nobuhiko Takada made his professional wrestling debut in 1981 against Norio Honaga, for New Japan Pro Wrestling, where he started his career as a Junior Heavyweight.","alterEgos":["Generalissimo Takada"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":51,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":69,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":49,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"picture":"Nobuhiko Takada.png"},{"id":1018,"name":"Animal Hamaguchi","realName":"Animal Hamaguchi","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":227,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1947-08-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1965-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":5,"charisma":100,"micSkills":100,"condition":44,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":71,"ability":99,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Heigo Hamaguchi is a Japanese retired professional wrestler, better known by the ring name Animal Hamaguchi.  During his career he was recognized as a talented tag team wrestler despite his small size for a heavyweight, and today he is recognized as a trainer in both professional and amateur wrestling. Hamaguchi debuted in 1969 in the old International Wrestling Enterprise. He was a regular mid-carder although his teams with Mighty Inoue and Rusher Kimura were main event. Hamaguchi retired in 1995, after his team lost the title, to dedicate full-time to his dojo, today recognized as one of the premier independent wrestling schools in Japan.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":90,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":92,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":38,"technicalCoaching":39,"characterCoaching":51,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":38,"consistency":49,"awareness":86,"judgement":92},"picture":"Animal Hamaguchi.png"},{"id":1019,"name":"Akira Hokuto","realName":"Akira Hokuto","nickname":"","type":"scout","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":139,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1967-07-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":18,"charisma":81,"micSkills":85,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":98,"injuryProne":30,"ability":99,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hisako Sasaki is a former professional wrestler better known as Akira Hokuto. She is married to wrestler Kensuke Sasaki. Akira was one of the most talented women wrestlers in the world, while active. She along with Kensuke, have taken in Katsuhiko Nakajima in as their almost adopted son. She also helps with the running of Diamond Ring (ex-Kensuke Office)","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":46,"storytelling":33,"productFit":20,"riskTaking":53,"matchLayout":42,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":40,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":42,"teaching":50,"diagnosis":35,"rehabilitation":36,"prevention":39,"mediaHandling":26,"brandBuilding":30,"socialMediaSavvy":43,"ruleKnowledge":49,"positioning":21,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":29,"awareness":33,"judgement":90},"picture":"Akira Hokuto.png"},{"id":1020,"name":"Obariyon","realName":"Obariyon","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":191,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1987-11-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":2,"charisma":50,"micSkills":45,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":100,"ability":58,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":57,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"The Batiri is a professional wrestling alliance in the Chikara promotion. The team currently includes Kobald, Kodama and Obariyon; the first performs under a goblin mask, while the latter two wear face paint with the wrestling characters of demons. Both Kodama's and Obariyon's ring names come from Japanese folklore from the characters of Kodama and Obariyon, while Kobald is named after the German word for goblin. All three men were trained at Chikara's Wrestle Factory by then head trainers Claudio Castagnoli and Mike Quackenbush. On August 28, 2010, Obariyon made his professional wrestling debut for the Chikara promotion, defeating Dustin Rayz in the first round of the Young Lions Cup VIII tournament.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[308,3221,3222],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":48,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":48,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":56,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":75,"awareness":56,"judgement":53},"picture":"Obariyon.png"},{"id":1021,"name":"Kodama","realName":"Kodama","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":185,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1982-07-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":2,"charisma":62,"micSkills":52,"condition":96,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":100,"ability":44,"currentAbility":36,"potentialAbility":38,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"The Batiri is a professional wrestling alliance in the Chikara promotion. The team currently includes Kobald, Kodama and Obariyon; the first performs under a goblin mask, while the latter two wear face paint with the wrestling characters of demons. Both Kodama's and Obariyon's ring names come from Japanese folklore from the characters of Kodama and Obariyon, while Kobald is named after the German word for goblin. All three men were trained at Chikara's Wrestle Factory by then head trainers Claudio Castagnoli and Mike Quackenbush. On September 18, Obariyon entered a four-way tag team match, teaming with the debuting Kodama, with the two wearing identical attire and face paint. The two were the second team eliminated from the match by The Osirian Portal.","alterEgos":["Louie Valle"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[308,3221,3222],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":56,"productFit":46,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":46,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":45,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":30,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":9,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":77,"awareness":53,"judgement":50},"picture":"Kodama.png"},{"id":1024,"name":"Onryo","realName":"Onryo","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":211,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1975-07-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":52,"micSkills":67,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"ability":64,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":46,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"An amateur wrestler at university, Onryo debuted as \"Wolf Ozawa\" in Wrestle Dream Factory, a ring name he would revive several years later. Onryo wrestled in FMW until his closure, then joined WMF. In 2003 he created with the Crazy SKB, \"666 Triplefiesta\", a bizarre indy promotion, which soon gathered fan interest. Onryo took part in the Super J Cup 2000 and was eliminated in the semifinals by CIMA. Despite never being a top wrestler in any promotion, Onryo was able to win some individual and tag team titles during his career. Onryo's character is inspired to a supernatural creature of the japanese folklore; an Onryo is a ghost who can return to the physical world seeking for vengeance.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":72,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":74,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":69,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"Onryo.png"},{"id":1025,"name":"Hagane Shinnou","realName":"Hagane Shinnou","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1983-12-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":69,"micSkills":74,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"ability":52,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":47,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hagane Shinnou is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with AEW, GanPro and Gatoh Move. He is currently the Super Asia champion.","alterEgos":["Madoka"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2953,3175],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":59,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":73,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"MADOKA.png"},{"id":1026,"name":"Ricochet","realName":"Ricochet","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":188,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1988-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":46,"charisma":68,"micSkills":66,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100,"ability":78,"currentAbility":78,"potentialAbility":93,"morale":"fair","presentation":"heel","prestige":"mid","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Ricochet is an American wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan, Europe and Oceania. He is a 5'9\", 188lb worker who is classed as using a High Flyer style. He uses the 630° Splash as his finisher. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NJPW, NXT, Dragon Gate, PWG, wXw, RevPro, Lucha Ungrnd, Beyond, EVOLVE, AAW, IWA-MS, Defiant, DTU, CHIKARA and CZW. He is engaged to someone outside the wrestling business. He was voted Male Independent Wrestler Of The Year in 2014.","alterEgos":["Prince Puma"],"birthplace":"Alton, Illinois, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1026","wrestlerId":1026,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2024-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1106,1219,1327,1647,2075,2704,3712],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":83,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":55,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":70,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":83,"consistency":80,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Ricochet.png"},{"id":1028,"name":"Cody Hall","realName":"Cody Hall","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":268,"height":205,"dateOfBirth":"1991-05-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":6,"charisma":54,"micSkills":37,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":33,"injuryProne":89,"ability":43,"currentAbility":42,"potentialAbility":42,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Cody Hall is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a Light Heavyweight who is classed as using a Powerhouse style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, AAA, NOAH, DDT, GWF, RevPro and TNT.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1001],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":40,"storytelling":45,"productFit":86,"riskTaking":52,"matchLayout":46,"psychology":40,"workerManagement":86,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":21,"characterCoaching":53,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":48,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":17,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":52,"awareness":40,"judgement":58},"picture":"Cody Hall.png"},{"id":1029,"name":"Arik Cannon","realName":"Arik Cannon","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":202,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1981-12-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":5,"charisma":52,"micSkills":54,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"ability":58,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Arik Cannon is a professional wrestler known for competing in companies such as Chikara, IWA Mid-South, All American Wrestling and Wrestling Society X. Arik Cannon was trained at Midwest Pro Wrestling and is known for wrestling in IWA Mid-South. There, he became the IWA Mid-South Heavyweight Champion by defeating Petey Williams in the Ted Petty Invitational Tournament. He defended it against Roderick Strong and Austin Aries, but was forced to give it up due to injury in 2004. He returned to wrestling in 2005 and entered Chikara's Tag World Grand Prix 2005 with partner Claudio Castagnoli and made it to the finals to face Superfriends, Chris Hero and Mike Quackenbush. On September 6, 2009, Cannon made his debut for Dragon Gate USA at the tapings of the promotion's second pay-per-view titled Untouchable.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2680],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":47,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":56,"psychology":47,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":78,"awareness":47,"judgement":68},"picture":"Arik Cannon.png"},{"id":1030,"name":"Lince Dorado","realName":"Lince Dorado","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":65,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":181,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1987-05-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-02-17T00:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":20,"charisma":61,"micSkills":37,"condition":85,"hardcor