by holding all three major NWA singles titles, The National, North American ,and Worlds Heavyweight Titles.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":36,"characterCoaching":55,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":75,"awareness":59,"judgement":75},"picture":"Kahagas.png"},{"id":1101,"name":"Yoshiaki Yatsu","realName":"Yoshiaki Yatsu","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":253,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1956-07-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1976-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":4,"charisma":80,"micSkills":100,"condition":54,"hardcoreAbility":92,"injuryProne":86,"ability":98,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"A veteran wrestler who has been active for over 30 years, Yatsu was originally an olympic freestyle wrestler who took part to the Montreal olympic games. After retiring, Yatsu immediately joined the New Japan Dojo and debuted in USA in the WWF. A couple of years later Yatsu finally had his Japanese debut, as a Riki Choshu protégé. In 1984 Yatsu left New Japan for All Japan, where he had a huge push, capturing the NWA International Tag Team Title when he teamed with Riki Choshu. In 1998/1999 Yatsu formed a successful tag team with Jumbo Tsuruta and they would win the All Japan Tag Team Championship 5 times. Following this success, Yatsu even had a title shot for the Triple Crown, but was defeated by Tenryu. In 1990 Yatsu joined SWS and when the promotion closed its doors in 1992, his career started to decline. He founded SPWF (Social Pro Wrestling Federation), which has never encountered a great deal of success.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2978,2979],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":44,"technicalCoaching":41,"characterCoaching":55,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":25,"positioning":40,"reactionSpeed":44,"consistency":49,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"picture":"Yoshiaki Yatsu.png"},{"id":1103,"name":"Azteca","realName":"Azteca","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":198,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1970-07-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":58,"micSkills":63,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":41,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Azteca is the co-founder of KAGEKI and a 16-year veteran of wrestling. He debuted in Mexico and competed throughout Japan before founding KAGEKI and becoming it’s leader and top star. He has maintained good relationships with some of puroresu’s top stars, which has opened the door not only for some KAGEKI stars to participate in other promotions, but for these big names to also appear in KAGEKI over the years.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":52,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":64,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":52,"consistency":73,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"Azteca.png"},{"id":1104,"name":"Kzy","realName":"Kzy","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1986-06-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":78,"micSkills":76,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":62,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kzy is a Japanese wrestler for Dragon Gate, where he is a member of the Real Hazard stable, Also goes by the ring name Mc.KZ. During 2006, he debuted during some Dragon Gate NEX shows as m.c.KZ. His gimmick was that of a rapper, and he rapped his own theme song on his way to the ring.\r\n","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":75,"awareness":67,"judgement":80},"picture":"Kzy.png"},{"id":1105,"name":"YAMATO","realName":"YAMATO","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":181,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1981-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":6,"charisma":78,"micSkills":89,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"ability":67,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":56,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"YAMATO, a 2006 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Mexico and Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with Dragongate.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1351,1575,2509],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":77,"characterCoaching":75,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":79,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"picture":"Yamato.png"},{"id":1106,"name":"Mondai Ryu","realName":"Mondai Ryu","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":275,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1983-01-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":48,"micSkills":60,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":34,"injuryProne":100,"ability":60,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":54,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"The wrestler formerly known as Super Shenlong until spring 2012, he was a masked wrestler who is supposed to be a Chinese wrestler in Dragon Gate. He is a NEX talent and lower-card wrestler who usually works opening matches and garnered a cult fan following because he’s the perennial underdog as well as be a hero to Chinese fans for trying to break through in Japan. During the major faction shifting of early 2012 Shenlong turned heel and changed his name to Mondai Ryu (the kanji loosely translates as “Problem Dragon”), aligning himself with Akira Tozawa’s MAD BLANKEY faction and antagonizing the faces and opposition, usually by throwing white powder in a bucket he carries around.","alterEgos":["Dr. Muscle"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":66,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":62,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"picture":"Mondai Ryu.png"},{"id":1107,"name":"Eddie Roberts","realName":"Eddie Roberts","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":164,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1993-02-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":0,"charisma":54,"micSkills":45,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":31,"injuryProne":100,"ability":41,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":47,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Eddie Roberts is a Scottish professional wrestling referee who works across Scotland.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Scotland","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":38,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":38,"brandBuilding":8,"socialMediaSavvy":25,"ruleKnowledge":49,"positioning":39,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Eddie Roberts.png"},{"id":1108,"name":"Jackie Polo","realName":"Jackie Polo","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":218,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1987-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":1,"charisma":50,"micSkills":63,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"ability":50,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"A dominating physical presence, Polo likes to focus on technical wrestling to wear down his opponents in addition to his ability to throw people around like rag dolls with his size and strength. His skills are shadowed only by his ego as Jackie Polo believes himself to be ‘Scotlands BEEEST wrestler’ and will tell that to anyone who crosses his path! Having tagged with Joe Coffey as Legitimate Threat, Polo found success in tag competition teaming with both Mark and Joe Coffey over the years but his quest to prove he is better than all others has led him to go solo in recent years, using his intensity and aggression to show can take on the best of the best and survive.","alterEgos":["JAXN"],"birthplace":"Scotland","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[861,1279],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":60,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":62,"awareness":56,"judgement":54},"picture":"Jackie Polo.png"},{"id":1109,"name":"Tamina","realName":"Tamina","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":169,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1978-01-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":27,"charisma":46,"micSkills":52,"condition":68,"hardcoreAbility":34,"injuryProne":99,"ability":43,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":32,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Sarona Reiher is an American professional wrestler and is the first female wrestler to come out of the Samoan Wrestling Family. She is the daughter of WWE Hall of Famer Jimmy \"Superfly\" Snuka and the younger sister of former WWE wrestler Deuce. Sarona first began in wrestling after she received the first Lia Maivia Scholarship to train in professional wrestling career at the Wild Samoan Training Center. On December 26, 2009 it was reported through WXW's official twitter account that WWE signed Reiher to a developmental contract and would report to their developmental territory Florida Championship Wrestling for further training.","alterEgos":["Sarona Snuka"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1243,2443,2771],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":58,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":53,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":50,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"picture":"Tamina.png"},{"id":1110,"name":"Bayley","realName":"Bayley","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":119,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1989-06-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":75000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":56,"charisma":79,"micSkills":84,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":80,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Long before she was a SmackDown LIVE Superstar, Bayley was a 10-year-old superfan in San Jose, Calif., watching her favorites like Lita and Eddie Guerrero on TV. She decided then that she wanted to inspire fans the same way the Superstars of the ’90s and early ’00s did for her.\r\n\r\nNot all that long ago, Bayley still aspired to do all those things, but late 2019 saw the former hugger undergo a jaw-dropping transformation from one of WWE’s most pure personalities into a win-at-all-costs, rule-breaking brawler.\r\n\r\nWhen she turned 18, Bayley started to train for the squared circle, and after learning the ropes on the indies, she joined NXT’s burgeoning Women’s division in 2012. Unlike her contemporaries, she didn’t mirror Charlotte’s confidence, Sasha Banks’ swagger or Becky Lynch’s toughness. Instead, Bayley had an ever-present smile and an overwhelming enthusiasm that made it impossible to root against her.","alterEgos":["Davina Rose"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1110","wrestlerId":1110,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":75000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1771,4285],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":83,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":82,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"picture":"Bayley.png"},{"id":1111,"name":"Joe Cabray","realName":"Joe Cabray","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":242,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1982-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":5,"charisma":75,"micSkills":83,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":90,"ability":72,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Luther Ward is no stranger to physicality. Building upon a proud lineage of Irish fighters, Ward views his place on NXT as a birthright. Need further evidence? One need not look further than the last name bestowed upon him by his father; “Ward” is defined as “Soldier of the People.” Since enduring the harshest of wrestling rings throughout Europe, Ward prides himself on being one of the toughest, most hardened and ruthless men to ever come to NXT. This highly disciplined Irish battler takes huge gratification in dismantling his opponents mentally and physically, piece by piece. Now that Ward has finally landed in NXT, his focus is to show the world that he is the toughest Irish man to ever live.","alterEgos":["Omen","Luther Ward"],"birthplace":"Ireland","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":42,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":62,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"picture":"Luther Ward.png"},{"id":1112,"name":"Genki Horiguchi","realName":"Genki Horiguchi","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1978-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":6,"charisma":72,"micSkills":66,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":52,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Genki Horiguchi, is a Japanese professional wrestler. He is currently a full time wrestler and booker for Dragon Gate. He has also competed in Wrestling Society X and Ring of Honor. When Horiguchi's hairline began receding, the fans began to chant H-A-G-E (Japanese for 'bald') at him. He managed to use this to gain a sort of cult popularity, and his catchphrase, \"Who has called me hage?\", is one of the best known in Japan. Horiguchi debuted in Toryumon as a face wrestler with a surfer gimmick. In 2001, he began to lose his hair, and in November he turned heel, cast away his surfer gimmick, and he joined the original M2K as a replacement for Chocoflake K-ICHI. He was the last wrestler to be added to the group.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1217],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":76,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":71,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"picture":"Genki Horiguchi.png"},{"id":1113,"name":"Dan Engler","realName":"Dan Engler","nickname":"","type":"referee","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1977-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":2,"charisma":83,"micSkills":86,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":51,"ability":78,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":59,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Dan Engler is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with WWE and TNA. He was voted Referee Of The Year in 2018.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Evansville, Indiana, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1113","wrestlerId":1113,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":51,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":1,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":79,"positioning":63,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Rudy Charles_alt2.png"},{"id":1114,"name":"Mike Posey","realName":"Mike Posey","nickname":"","type":"referee","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":145,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1977-08-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":1,"charisma":68,"micSkills":63,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":83,"injuryProne":100,"ability":73,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"The Birmingham, AL native performed as a wrestler and referee initially in Alabama & Georgia, most notably for NWA Wildside. He joined TNA as a referee, and also wrestled in a feud with David Young as \"Dropkick\" Posey. He resigned from TNA to try-out for WWE and after several dark matches was the 1st referee to join WWE's development promotion Deep South Wrestling, initially without a WWE contract. Soon he was signed. When the ECW brand was launched he joined the WWE roster as one of its refs, eventually becoming the brand's Sr. official. In his time in WWE he was a ref in matches on all three WWE brands and appeared at two WrestleManias. Returning to wrestling in 2009, Mike Posey teamed with former WWE Referee, Wes Adams, as the Official Express and Corey Hollis as Alabama Attitude in ROH. Posey won numerous singles titles.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1114","wrestlerId":1114,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[327],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":34,"storytelling":42,"productFit":70,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":44,"psychology":34,"workerManagement":70,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":53,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":70,"positioning":70,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":73,"awareness":34,"judgement":48},"picture":"Mike Posey.png"},{"id":1115,"name":"Petey Williams","realName":"Petey Williams","nickname":"","type":"writer","promotionId":64,"base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":179,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1981-08-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":12,"charisma":77,"micSkills":91,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":100,"ability":90,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Petey Williams, a 2002 graduate of the Can-Am Wrestling School, is a retired Canadian wrestler who works primarily as a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT, PWG, AJPW, ROH, HOH, Smash, IWA-MS, C4 and CZW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He is the protege of Scott D'Amore. He was voted Young Wrestler Of The Year in 2004.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Windsor, Ontario, Canada","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1115","wrestlerId":1115,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":63,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":73,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Petey Williams_alt2.png"},{"id":1117,"name":"William Grange","realName":"William Grange","nickname":"","type":"commentator","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":196,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1987-11-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":1,"charisma":14,"micSkills":22,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":100,"ability":12,"currentAbility":11,"potentialAbility":11,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"William Grange is a Scottish professional wrestler. Grange has always viewed himself as being better than anyone else. He believes he is the most inteligent man in ICW and it is his God given right to have ICW gold around his waist. With his tag partner Dickie Divers, he is a member of STI, one of the top teams in ICW. Currently embroiled in a fued with the Bucky Boys, Grange deplores the Bucky Boys, the Wee Man in particlaur as he sees them as everything that is wrong with today's society. Voted ICW Best Talker 2011, Grange is never short of words and has said the most controversial things ever uttered in a wrestling ring.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Scotland","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":54,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":73,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":67,"awareness":53,"judgement":52},"picture":"William Grange.png"},{"id":1118,"name":"John Myers","realName":"John Myers","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":204,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1983-06-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":0,"charisma":52,"micSkills":41,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":0,"ability":44,"currentAbility":37,"potentialAbility":37,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDeve