nd Japan. He is a 6'0\", 213lb worker who is classed as using a Brawler style. He uses the Buckshot Lariat as his finisher. He is best known for his work with AEW, NJPW, PWG, ROH and EVOLVE. He is currently the AEW World champion.","alterEgos":["Hangman Page"],"birthplace":"Halifax County, Virginia, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1231","wrestlerId":1231,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":80000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[652,1269,1968],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":85,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":85,"socialMediaSavvy":83,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":83,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"picture":"Adam Page.png"},{"id":1232,"name":"Naruki Doi","realName":"Naruki Doi","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":181,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1980-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":6,"charisma":64,"micSkills":57,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":54,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Naruki Doi is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico, Japan and Oceania. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with IMPACT, NOAH, Dragongate, DDT, PWG, ROH, AJPW and IWRG. He is currently the AJPW World Junior Heavyweight champion and the DDT Universal champion.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1032,1211,2509,3629,4020],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":83,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"picture":"Naruki Doi.png"},{"id":1233,"name":"Takashi","realName":"Takashi Yoshida","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":265,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1982-07-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":53,"micSkills":48,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"ability":56,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":48,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Takashi Yoshida is a Japanese wrestler, previously and best known by the ring name Cyber Kong. Cyber Kong's career started in 2006. He competed as an arm wrestler and was part of the New Japan Dojo system. He trained in the Los Angeles-based Inoki Dojo, but his short stature prevented him from getting far in it, so he took a tryout at the Dragon Gate USA dojo and became its first graduate. His frightening power, wrestling abilities, and muscular build made him nearly unbeatable in NEX, and thus he was soon brought up to the main roster, where he continued to be a major threat (however, he has shown himself to be susceptible to flash pins). On May 5th, 2017, Kong failed to capture the Open the Dream Gate Championship from YAMATO in a Steel Cage 5-Way Survival match, being the last man eliminated. As a result of the stipulation, he was forced to unmask, which eventually prompted him to reveal his real name and place of birth, officially bringing the Cyber Kong character to an end.","alterEgos":["Takashi Yoshida","Cyber Kong"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1575,2453,2949],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":40,"characterCoaching":44,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":67,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"picture":"Takashi Yoshida.png"},{"id":1234,"name":"Masato Yoshino","realName":"Masato Yoshino","nickname":"","type":"trainer","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":163,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1980-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"popularity":7,"charisma":87,"micSkills":98,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":92,"injuryProne":100,"ability":77,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Masato Yoshino is a retired Japanese wrestler who works as an on-screen personality and a road agent. He was one half of DoiYoshi alongside Naruki Doi. He is best known for his work with AAA, IMPACT, Dragongate, PWG, ROH and GLEAT.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[932,1032,3629],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":29,"productFit":22,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":26,"psychology":39,"workerManagement":59,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":92,"diagnosis":39,"rehabilitation":35,"prevention":48,"mediaHandling":39,"brandBuilding":57,"socialMediaSavvy":57,"ruleKnowledge":38,"positioning":46,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":53,"awareness":33,"judgement":55},"picture":"Masato Yoshino.png"},{"id":1235,"name":"Yasushi Kanda","realName":"Yasushi Kanda","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":187,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1978-08-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":66,"micSkills":54,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":84,"ability":56,"currentAbility":42,"potentialAbility":44,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hiroyuki Kanda, better known as Yasushi Kanda, born on August 29, 1978 in Inage-ku, Chiba, Japan, is a Japanese wrestler currently performing for the Dragon Gate wrestling promotion in Japan. He is considered one of Toryumon's greatest heel characters, and was a founding member of the M2K stable. In his pre-injury days, he was famous for his mohawk hairstyle. Kanda was trained by Ultimo Dragon as a 2nd Term student. Shortly after debuting, he allied with Susumu Mochizuki. He suffered a legitimate neck injury on October 10, 2001 after taking a back-to-belly piledriver from Genki Horiguchi that displaced his neck vertebrae. He shifted over to a referee job. In 2006, Don Fujii of heel stable Blood Generation began to harass Kanda during matches. Kanda was provoked into fighting back. His full return to the ring occurred in July 2006, when he signed a wrestler's contract.","alterEgos":["Jimmy Kanda"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1116],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":41,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":57,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":44,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":59,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":36,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":54,"positioning":63,"reactionSpeed":57,"consistency":55,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"picture":"Yasushi Kanda.png"},{"id":1236,"name":"KAGETORA","realName":"KAGETORA","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":179,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1982-04-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":67,"micSkills":61,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":40,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":53,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Fumiyuki Hashimoto known by his stage name Kagetora (stylized as KAGETORA), is a Japanese professional wrestler who works for Dragon Gate. He wrestles in independent wrestling leagues all around Japan and has wrestled in the United States for Chikara and Pro Wrestling Guerrilla. He has wrestled many famous wrestlers including Jinsei Shinzaki. Hashimoto was part of Mini Crazy MAX as SUWAcito early in his career with Takuya Sugi (Mini CIMA) and Masaki Okimoto (Small Dandy Fuji). They were little version of the Japanese wrestlers CIMA, Suwa and Don Fujii. On December 19, 2008, KAGETORA debuted in Dragon Gate after it was announced that El Dorado would be closing, intruding after the opening match. He openly declared war on Dragon Gate, attacking m.c. KZ and criticizing fellow former El Dorado wrestler Naoki Tanisaki for abandoning the company months prior.","alterEgos":["Jimmy Kagetora"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1117,2945],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":47,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":50,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":67,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Kagetora.png"},{"id":1237,"name":"Susumu Yokosuka","realName":"Susumu Yokosuka","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":170,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1978-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":8,"charisma":58,"micSkills":56,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":52,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Susumu Mochizuki better known by his ring name Susumu Yokosuka (born August 18, 1978) is a Japanese professional wrestler currently performing for the Dragon Gate professional wrestling promotion. He is not related to fellow Dragon Gate wrestler and long term ally/rival Masaaki Mochizuki, who debuted much earlier for WAR. After a brief stay in the Michinoku Pro Wrestling dojo, he entered Ultimo Dragon's dojo in Mexico. He debuted in 1998 as a third term student. On Dragon Gate USA's first pay-per-view Enter the Dragon, first aired on September 4, 2009, Yokosuka teamed with CIMA in a losing effort against The Young Bucks.","alterEgos":["Jimmy Susumu","Susumu Mochizuki"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1116,1117,1145,2946],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":76,"awareness":67,"judgement":80},"picture":"Susumu Mochizuki.png"},{"id":1238,"name":"Naoki Tanizaki","realName":"Naoki Tanizaki","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":172,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1978-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":41,"micSkills":44,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"ability":59,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":46,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Naoki Tanizaki is a Japanese wrestler currently competing for Dragon Gate. Originally from the Toryumon X promotion, Naoki Tanizaki debuted in a Toryumon Mexico show in December 2002. When Toryumon X made their Japanese landing in August 2003, Naoki debuted as a surfer (similar to Genki Horiguchi) defeating Kenichi Hanai. Tanizaki quickly joined the El Dorado Wrestling roster, even though he continued to remain a freelance wrestler. He was out injured after his second match with the company, however. He joined up with Shuji Kondo upon returning. Parts of his freelancing included forays into Pro Wrestling ZERO1-MAX, Big Japan Pro Wrestling and Kaientai Dojo. In the latter, he joined the heel stable Omega. In 2008, he resigned from El Dorado.","alterEgos":["Mr. Kyu Kyu Naoki Tanizaki"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":39,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":52,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":71,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":61,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":57,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":67,"awareness":52,"judgement":71},"picture":"Naoki Tanizaki.png"},{"id":1239,"name":"Ryo Saito","realName":"Ryo Saito","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1979-08-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":7,"charisma":53,"micSkills":79,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"ability":55,"currentAbility":42,"potentialAbility":44,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Ryo Saito is a Japanese professional wrestler, also known by the ring name Ryo \"Jimmy\" Saito. He wrestles for Dragon Gate, where he is a member of the Jimmyz stable. His name is sometimes abbreviated as SaiRyo, so as not to confuse him with Toryumon/DG alumni SAITO.  Ryo Saito debuted in 1999 as a fourth term student. He fought in that year's Young Dragons Cup, but lost in the finals to the newly-heel Yasushi Kanda. In 2000, he would divide his time between Japan and Mexico, and in Japan he adopted the gimmick of a bicycling enthusiast, wearing a professional bicycler’s outfit, helmet, and glasses and coming to the ring on a bicycle. Saito turned heel on January 14, 2011, along with the rest of WARRIORS, when they attacked Masato Yoshino and World-1, and joined forces with Naruki Doi's group.","alterEgos":["Ryo \"Jimmy\" Saito"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[618,1217,2946],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":74,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":67,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Ryo Saito.png"},{"id":1240,"name":"Don Fujii","realName":"Don Fujii","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1970-07-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":53,"micSkills":58,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":100,"ability":53,"currentAbility":31,"potentialAbility":33,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Tatsuki Fuji is a Japanese wrestler for Dragon Gate, best known by his ring name Don Fujii. He was one-half of the inaugural Open the Owarai Twin Gate Champions and is also a former two-time Open the Twin Gate Champions with Masaaki Mochizuki. He was previously in the Crazy MAX and Blood Generation stables. He was one of the original graduates from the Toryumon dojo. He was also one of the founding members of the Crazy MAX & Blood Generation stables. He made a few appearances in World Championship Wrestling as Sumo Fuji. He has wrestled as Karaoke Machine #1 at times as well. From 1999 until 2002, he changed his name annually.","alterEgos":["Sumo Dandy Fuji","Karaoke Machine #1","Strong Machine F"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[618,1582],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":47,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":52,"technicalCoaching":52,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":53,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":52,"consistency":67,"awareness":57,"judgement":74},"picture":"Don Fujii.png"},{"id":1241,"name":"Gamma","realName":"Gamma","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1973-05-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":64,"micSkills":47,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"ability":55,"currentAbility":36,"potentialAbility":38,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yoshito Sugamoto is a Japanese professional wrestler, better known by the ring name Gamma. He is currently working for the Dragon Gate promotion. Yoshito Sugamoto began his career in Michinoku Pro when he entered their dojo, where he often wrestled in dark matches. He then left for Osaka Pro, where he gained top heel status. When he left that promotion, he toured the Japanese independent circuit, appearing briefly in dragondoor and in the STONED stable in El Dorado. He eventually turned up in Dragon Gate on March 19, 2006, being brought in by his friend Magnitude Kishiwada to take over his position in Blood Generation while he recuperated from a severe shoulder injury. He and stable head CIMA took an instant dislike to each other, however, and he was soon kicked out of the faction.","alterEgos":["Viewtiful Joe"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1266],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":72,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":61,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"GAMMA.png"},{"id":1242,"name":"Super Shisa","realName":"Super Shisa","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":169,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1970-04-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":66,"micSkills":49,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":55,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":37,"potentialAbility":39,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yoshiyuki Saito is a Japanese professional wrestler best known by his ring name Super Shisa, currently wrestling for Dragon Gate. His gimmick is inspired by the Ryukyuan Shisa. He claimed to be a student of Toryumon alumni SAITO, but was outed as being SAITO himself in 2007. Saito got his start in wrestling with Último Dragón's upstart promotion Toryumon. He trained in Mexico with the rest of the Último Dragón students, and briefly used the Super Shisa gimmick while there. He wrestled January 31, 1999, on Toryumon's debut show. Wrestling under his real name, he teamed with Magnum Tokyo and Dragon Kid to take on Shima Nobunaga, Sumo Fuji and Judo Suwa in an elimination match on the main event of the card. Saito would be eliminated second following a Nodowa Elbow from Fuji, but his team would go on to win the match.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2948],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":66,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":54,"awareness":67,"judgement":80},"picture":"Super Shisa.png"},{"id":1243,"name":"Dragon Kid","realName":"Dragon Kid","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":154,"height":160,"dateOfBirth":"1976-02-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":7,"charisma":68,"micSkills":51,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":100,"ability":55,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":41,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Dragon Kid is a masked Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico and Japan. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a Luchador style. He is best known for his work with Dragongate.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1031,1034,2006,2944,4020],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":72,"awareness":72,"judgement":83},"picture":"Dragon Kid.png"},{"id":1244,"name":"K-ness","realName":"K-ness","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":163,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1974-04-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":5,"charisma":64,"micSkills":61,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":55,"injuryProne":100,"ability":64,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Makoto Saito, better known by his stage name K-ness is a Japanese professional wrestler for Dragon Gate. He debuted in Michinoku Pro around the same time as Gamma, and then went on to wrestle on the Japanese indy circuit. He joined Toryumon in 1999 as MAKOTO, with a vampire style gimmick. As MAKOTO he was a member of the legendary Crazy Max stable. However, he did not get along with TARU, and eventually was kicked out of the stable after losing to TARU in a loser leaves match. In November 2003 he suffered a major shoulder injury which caused him to miss out on the majority of 2004, and the switch from Toryumon to Dragon Gate. By the time K-ness returned, Ultimo Dragon had left the promotion and taken the Toryumon trademark with him.","alterEgos":["Darkness Dragon","Jimmy K-Ness JKS!"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1031,1145],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":59,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":72,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"K-Ness.png"},{"id":1245,"name":"Magnitude Kishiwada","realName":"Magnitude Kishiwada","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":198,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1971-05-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":42,"micSkills":59,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":74,"injuryProne":100,"ability":60,"currentAbility":37,"potentialAbility":39,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Toyonari Fujita better known as Magnitude Kishiwada, is a Japanese wrestler. He wrestles for the Dragon Gate promotion. During his highschool life, Fujita trained in artistic gymnastics and powerlifting, and years later, he showed interest in professional wrestling. For many years Fujita trained in worked in preliminary matches in Japan's hardcore wrestling promotions, including FMW, W*ING, and Big Japan Pro Wrestling, competing under his real name, and as Toryu. He eventually landed in Osaka Pro, where he became a kaiju character named Monster Zeta Mandora. However, he gained fame in early 2002 by turning heel and renaming himself, Big Boss MA-G-MA.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":47,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":22,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":49,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"picture":"Magnitude Kishiwada.png"},{"id":1246,"name":"Masaaki Mochizuki","realName":"Masaaki Mochizuki","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":187,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1970-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":6,"charisma":65,"micSkills":68,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":38,"potentialAbility":40,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Masaaki Mochizuki is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently performing for Dragon Gate and its international expansion Dragon Gate USA. He hosted his self-produced show, Buyuden. A graduate of Koji Kitao's Buko Dojo, Masaaki spent the early part of his career wrestling for various promotions across Japan, namely WAR and BattlARTS. Most notable was his appearance in the 1995 Super J Cup, where he took on Shinjiro Otani of New Japan Pro Wrestling in the first round. Despite losing, Masaaki looked very competitive, using his sharp kicks and quick submission holds to pose a serious threat to the more experienced Otani. In December, he celebrated 10 years in wrestling by defeating CIMA for Dragon Gate's top prize, the Open the Dream Gate Championship. He held the title for 11 months before losing it to Magnitude Kishiwada on November 4, 2005. When 2006 rolled around, he began to distance himself from Final M2K a bit.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1555,1582,2453,3999,4000],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":58,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":71,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"picture":"Masaaki Mochizuki.png"},{"id":1247,"name":"Akira Tozawa","realName":"Akira Tozawa","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":156,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1985-07-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":30,"charisma":74,"micSkills":48,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"ability":60,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":73,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Inside the ring and out, Akira Tozawa is an audacious Superstar. As the third-ever graduate of Japan’s world-respected Dragon Gate dojo, Tozawa helped blaze a trail as an early staple of the Dragon Gate organization. Yet, Tozawa’s vicious strikes have been felt worldwide, courtesy of several tours around the globe. Along the way, the trash-talking, fearless fighter has crossed paths with the likes of Kevin Owens, Dean Ambrose and Sami Zayn. Tozawa has unleashed his unique brand of brutality, including a big boot that leaves its imprint via countless kick varieties and enough German suplexes to make Brock Lesnar proud. With agility and athleticism to spare, no opponent is safe from his far-reaching bicycle kick.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Nishinomiya, Hyogo, Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1247","wrestlerId":1247,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[921,1229,1256,4071],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":87,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":76,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":87,"consistency":73,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"picture":"Akira Tozawa.png"},{"id":1248,"name":"Taku Iwasa","realName":"Taku Iwasa","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":198,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1978-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":62,"micSkills":59,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":99,"ability":49,"currentAbility":37,"potentialAbility":37,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Taku Iwasa is a Japanese professional wrestler who currently wrestles for Dragon Gate. Iwasa graduated as part of the Toryumon T2P class. He initially portrayed Takamichi Iwasa, a Satanic character. Injuries derailed his career, and he soon ended up as a jobber to the stars. He was briefly scouted by the famous Crazy MAX stable, and they gave him a ten match trial series. CMAX was never truly interested in Iwasa, though, and he lost all 10 matches. Following this, he joined forces with Raimu Mishima, who had been exiled from M2K for losing too many matches and general weakness. They petitioned to form their own unit, but were unable to do so. They then left for America to undergo Warrior Training. In mid-2009, Iwasa abruptly announced his retirement. On March 1, 2011, Iwasa announced that he would be making a return from his 18 month hiatus. Iwasa never returned to a full time wrestling schedule. He has not wrestled since 2012, although he maintains his spot on the Dragon Gate roster.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[935],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":49,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":49,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":51,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":22,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"picture":"Taku Iwasa.png"},{"id":1250,"name":"Takayuki Yagi","realName":"Takayuki Yagi","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1975-05-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"popularity":2,"charisma":64,"micSkills":53,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":57,"ability":76,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Takayuki Yagi is a referee and former wrestler for Dragon Gate. Yagi joined the Toryumon system as a part of the T2P class. He started his career under his real name, and his initial gimmick was that of a fisherman who carried a large flag with a sea-oriented design to the ring. Following the formation of the Italian Connection on March 3, 2002, he was accepted into the unit and renamed Pescatore Yagi, \"pescatore\" being the Italian word for fisherman, and he began carrying a large Italian flag to the ring instead. Yagi's in-ring career would end as part of the unnamed ItaCon breakaway faction. Yagi returned to Dragon Gate, but as a referee rather than a wrestler. It is presumed that he stepped down because of injury.\r\nHis first role as a referee was that of a face referee who was continually bothered by the antics of the Florida Brothers.","alterEgos":["Johnson Florida"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":20,"storytelling":29,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":77,"matchLayout":32,"psychology":20,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":41,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":56,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":23,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":68,"positioning":74,"reactionSpeed":41,"consistency":44,"awareness":20,"judgement":52},"picture":"Takayuki Yagi.png"},{"id":1251,"name":"Eita","realName":"Eita","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":45,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1991-10-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":7,"charisma":73,"micSkills":56,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":70,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Eita, a 2011 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in Mexico and Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, NOAH, Dragon Gate, IWRG, EVOLVE, FCP and DTU.","alterEgos":["Eita Kobayashi"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1251","wrestlerId":1251,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2022-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1224],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":78,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":56,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Eita.png"},{"id":1252,"name":"T-Hawk","realName":"T-Hawk","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":194,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1990-04-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":8,"charisma":80,"micSkills":59,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"ability":57,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":60,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"T-Hawk, a 2010 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, AEW, DDT, Dragongate, BJW, AJPW, wXw, GLEAT, IWRG, WRESTLE-1, EVOLVE and DTU.","alterEgos":["Tomahawk TT","Mr. Pii Pii Tomakomai Penguin"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1224,3542,3977],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":77,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"T-Hawk.png"},{"id":1253,"name":"Syachihoko BOY","realName":"Syachihoko BOY","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":198,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1980-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":3,"charisma":53,"micSkills":45,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":99,"ability":45,"currentAbility":36,"potentialAbility":38,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"BOY entered the system around the same time as Masato Yoshino. The two are contemporaries and remain close friends to this day. After debuting with Dragon Gate as Shachihoko Machine, he also began competing as Shisa BOY. He continued to do both characters for several years, although it eventually became obvious it was him under both masks. During a November 2011 Triangle Gate match, his Shachihoko mask was removed and he was sent to the backstage area. He returned with the Shisa BOY mask. From that time forward, he would occasionally appear with the characters mixed up. He formally fused them in the summer of 2012, becoming Shachihoko BOY. Shisa BOY & Shachihoko Machine appear to be sealed for the time being. His hard work improving his physical conditioning paid off in late 2012 when he was promoted from his Window spot to WORLD-1 International. He followed best friend Masato Yoshino to Monster Express.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[932,2948],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":44,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":49,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":56,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":47,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"picture":"Shachi Boi.png"},{"id":1254,"name":"U-T","realName":"U-T","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":154,"height":160,"dateOfBirth":"1993-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":43,"micSkills":57,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":77,"ability":48,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":54,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"U-T was scheduled to debut under his real name on 12tth April 2013 in his hometown of Nagoya. Less than 24 hours before the match, Eita sent a message to the DG office and the fans stating that Tanaka had accepted his solicitation to come train in Mexico. In doing so he became the first member of the roster to debut in Mexico since the Toryumon X class. His new identity was revealed during the first Millenials video. He was now U-T.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":63,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":56,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"U-T.png"},{"id":1255,"name":"Yosuke<3Santa Maria","realName":"Yosuke<3Santa Maria","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":161,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1991-12-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":61,"micSkills":50,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"ability":53,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":57,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Part of the 2011 debut class, Yosuke became the 3rd generation incarnation of the Super Shenlong character in 2012. After losing his mask in 2013, he briefly competed under his real name. No longer wanting to hide his feelings, he asked to join the Millenial so he could be with the man he loved, Eita. He underwent a shocking transformation, letting his true self shine through.","alterEgos":["Super Shenlong"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":68,"awareness":61,"judgement":77},"picture":"YosukeSanta Maria.png"},{"id":1256,"name":"Ken'ichiro Arai","realName":"Ken'ichiro Arai","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1972-07-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":55,"micSkills":48,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":55,"injuryProne":100,"ability":47,"currentAbility":30,"potentialAbility":32,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Keni'chiro Arai is a Japanese wrestler for Dragon Gate. Keni'chiro Arai, also known as AraKen, is a second term graduate of Último Dragón's Toryumon Japan group, and has been a mainstay on the roster ever since. He participated in FMW before joining Toryumon. He debuted as a heel, but turned face within the year and remained so for over a decade. On October 13, 2010, the Deep Drunkers lost a six man tag team match to World-1 and were as a result forced to split up. However, following the match World-1 member Naruki Doi turned on his stablemates and joined the former Deep Drunkers and Takuya Sugawara to form a new heel group. They however decided that Arai was not needed in the new group and kicked him out.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[935,2937],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":59,"characterCoaching":64,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":75,"awareness":57,"judgement":74},"picture":"Kenichiro Arai.png"},{"id":1257,"name":"Kotoka","realName":"Kotoka","nickname":"","type":"manager","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":145,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1990-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":6,"charisma":45,"micSkills":42,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":98,"ability":34,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":32,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"CIBA is lone survivor of the 2009 NEX class. After debuting under his real name, he was granted entry to WORLD-1. In a bit of irony, he was asked by his stablemates to shorten his ringname to simply Kotoka. The reason being that his last name Shiiba was too similar to CIMA. He felt insulted by being left out of the match that forced the end of W1, so he remained independent during the BW vs. JIII war. Rejected by the units that formed in the aftermath, he allied with the Windows group. He felt he fit in with them, since he was already being passed over for less experienced members by the other units. He formed a bond with CIMA during an excursion to Russia. This lead to him being bestowed the costume and offense of the DG ace. He began competing as CIBA. He also works as a regular reporter for the ABC Television morning news show Ohayou Asahi Desu.","alterEgos":["CIBA"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":48,"storytelling":57,"productFit":60,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":48,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":61,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":53,"awareness":48,"judgement":53},"picture":"Kotoka.png"},{"id":1258,"name":"Takayuki Mori","realName":"Takayuki Mori","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":154,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1976-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"popularity":3,"charisma":87,"micSkills":99,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":71,"ability":93,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Takayuki Mori  is a retired Japanese professional wrestler, better known by the ring name Anthony W. Mori. He is best known for working for Dragon Gate. Mori debuted with the Toryumon T2P class in 2000 under his real name. The following year, he became KENtaro Mori, \"Barbie's boyfriend\", and the year after that, he switched over to his current gimmick of Anthony W. Mori, a royal prince. Mori wrestled his retirement match on December 2, 2010. He remains with Dragon Gate in a backstage role.","alterEgos":["Anthony W. Mori"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":47,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"picture":"Anthony W Mori.png"},{"id":1259,"name":"Mikey Whipwreck","realName":"Mikey Whipwreck","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":180,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1973-06-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":4,"charisma":75,"micSkills":64,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":91,"injuryProne":71,"ability":67,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":44,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"John Watson  is an American professional wrestler, better known by his ring name Mikey Whipwreck. He is best known for his career with Extreme Championship Wrestling, where he became the third ECW Triple Crown Champion. Before becoming a professional wrestler, Whipwreck joined Extreme Championship Wrestling and was part of their ring crew, who would usually work for free as long as they could have fun in the ring themselves before and after shows had finished.  Booker Paul Heyman asked Mikey to wrestle competitively in ECW after he watched Whipwreck practice a variety of aerial maneuvers before a live show began. In early 2001, Whipwreck announced his intention to retire in May 2002 if he was not hired by the World Wrestling Federation, expressing an interest in pursuing a career in pyrotechnics. By June 11 he had decided to retire by September of that year, as his wrestling style had begun resulting in a number of nagging injuries.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2887,3246],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":50,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":50,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":51,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":38,"awareness":50,"judgement":70},"picture":"Mikey Whipwreck.png"},{"id":1260,"name":"Brandon Tolle","realName":"Brandon Tolle","nickname":"","type":"referee","promotionId":28,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":157,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1985-07-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":1,"charisma":59,"micSkills":51,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":33,"ability":54,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":50,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Brandon Tolle began his journey into the wrestling industry on his 18th birthday in 2003, after meeting his trainer Russell Jones in 2003 in Cincinnati. He began by training to be a wrestler, but after refereeing for a promotion in southern Kentucky when a referee was needed, he found out that refereeing was a better fit for him. He then began the task of mastering the craft that is being a Professional Wrestling Referee. Since that time Brandon has worked for over 25 different companies throughout the United States and Canada. Brandon is continually working to be the best that there is in the wrestling business when it comes to referees and will not stop until he is living his dream of working for WWE or TNA. Brandon has worked for companies such as Dragon Gate USA, Ring of Honor, The National Wrestling Alliance based out of Charlotte, NC, NWA Championship Wrestling from Hollywood, Insanity Pro Wrestling, Prime Time Wrestling, Maximum Pro Wrestling, Border City Wrestling and more.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1260","wrestlerId":1260,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2019-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":23,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":23,"brandBuilding":22,"socialMediaSavvy":12,"ruleKnowledge":64,"positioning":51,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Brandon Tolle.png"},{"id":1261,"name":"Shane McMahon","realName":"Shane McMahon","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":230,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1970-01-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":51,"charisma":48,"micSkills":49,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":95,"ability":48,"currentAbility":28,"potentialAbility":60,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Born with sports-entertainment in his blood, Shane McMahon has thrilled the WWE Universe with his daredevil decisions both in and out of the ring.\r\n\r\nThe only son of WWE Chairman Mr. McMahon, Shane grew up in sports-entertainment, learning the ins and outs of the business while holding various positions, including referee and announcer. In fact, Shane was the play-by-play man on the debut edition of Sunday Night Heat in 1999.\r\n\r\nIt wasn’t until the younger McMahon stepped out from behind the microphone that the WWE Universe saw how like his father he was, yet different in many ways. There’s no doubt that Shane McMahon inherited his father’s entrepreneurial spirit. However, he put a modern twist on it. He eschewed a suit and tie for a more casual look, not unlike contemporary moguls like Mark Cuban. His flamboyant, cocky attitude could be both endearing and irritating.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":55,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":57,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":26,"characterCoaching":72,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":43,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":55,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"Shane McMahon.png"},{"id":1262,"name":"Kazushi Miyamoto","realName":"Kazushi Miyamoto","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":260,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1979-02-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":5,"charisma":52,"micSkills":68,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":34,"injuryProne":100,"ability":56,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":45,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kazushi Miyamoto  will forever have the distinction of being the first post-split graduate of the All Japan Pro Wrestling dojo. While in the Dojo Miyamoto was trained by Hiroshi Hase, Johnny Smith, and his mentor Toshiaki Kawada. Miyamoto was so serious about wrestling for All Japan, he originally asked Giant Baba in 1996, but was denied due to his young age. After completing training in the Dojo, Miyamoto debuted on August 19, 2001 against Hiroshi Hase. A Jr. Heavyweight when he debuted, for the remainder of the year he opened cards and wrestled different veterans to help him hone his craft. He started 2002 off by pickingup his first pinfall victory in a tag team match, and a couple days later he had his first singles victory over Yasu Urano. For the rest of 2002 he continued wrestling towards the beginning of the card, waiting for his chance to elevate to a more meaningful role.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3044],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":38,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":38,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":55,"awareness":53,"judgement":72},"picture":"Kazushi Miyamoto.png"},{"id":1263,"name":"HUB","realName":"HUB","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1978-08-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":46,"micSkills":60,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"ability":51,"currentAbility":38,"potentialAbility":40,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"HUB is a Japanese wrestler who has worked for Osaka Pro, Dragon Gate and AJPW among others. He was trained by Super Delfin and has gone by many names over his many years in the business, such as GOA, Super Dolphin and Zero among others.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2891],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":58,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":62,"awareness":51,"judgement":71},"picture":"HUB.png"},{"id":1264,"name":"Kento Miyahara","realName":"Kento Miyahara","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":3,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":225,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1989-02-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":8,"charisma":86,"micSkills":88,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"ability":84,"currentAbility":79,"potentialAbility":84,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kento Miyahara is a Japanese wrestler who works in Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NOAH, Dragongate, DDT, BJW, AJPW, FREEDOMS and IWRG. He is currently the Triple Crown Heavyweight champion. He is the protege of Kensuke Sasaki.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1264","wrestlerId":1264,"promotionId":3,"startDate":"2014-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1696,2143,2301,3055,3665],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":91,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":88,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":88,"brandBuilding":88,"socialMediaSavvy":71,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":91,"consistency":86,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"picture":"Kento Miyahara_alt1.png"},{"id":1265,"name":"Hibiscus Mii","realName":"Hibiscus Mii","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":114,"height":149,"dateOfBirth":"1985-06-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":2,"charisma":44,"micSkills":46,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"ability":53,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"comedy","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"counter","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hibiscus Mii is a female professional wrestler, who currently works for Ryukyu Dragon Pro Wrestling. She is better known under her previous ring name Apple Miyuki under which she worked mainly for the Kaientai Dojo and Osaka Pro Wrestling promotions. She debuted on January 14, 2002, in Puerto Rico against another Kaientai Dojo wrestler, Ofune. 2007 saw a change for Apple, as with GET and RAVE being combined together. She had a small feud with Yu Yamagata to see who was the top women's wrestler in K-Dojo. They had two matches against each other, splitting them both, before throwing away their differences, and they have yet to have had a third singles match. In March 2013, Miyuki announced that she was joining the new Ryukyu Dragon Pro Wrestling promotion, adopting the new ring name Hibiscus Mii in the process.","alterEgos":["Apple Miyuki","Cosmic Warrior Justine"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3427],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":73,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":75,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Apple Miyuki_alt2.png"},{"id":1266,"name":"Yuzuki Aikawa","realName":"Yuzuki Aikawa","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":102,"height":154,"dateOfBirth":"1983-05-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":5,"charisma":45,"micSkills":51,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":33,"injuryProne":100,"ability":51,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yuzuki Aikawa is a Japanese gravure idol and retired professional wrestler. Starting her modeling career in 2003, Aikawa went on to become one of Japan's top gravure idols, earning the nickname \"The Gravure Queen of the Next Generation\" by appearing in various men's magazines, advertising campaigns, films, television programs and video games. In 2010, Aikawa transitioned into professional wrestling, joining the newly founded World Wonder Ring Stardom promotion, becoming its public face and the inaugural holder of the Wonder of Stardom and Goddesses of Stardom Championships. Aikawa's first year in professional wrestling ended with the Tokyo Sports magazine naming her the 2011 female wrestler of the year. A year later, having successfully defended the Wonder of Stardom Championship throughout the year, while also winning the inaugural 5Star GP, Aikawa became the first wrestler to win the award two times in a row.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3317],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":62,"productFit":23,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":23,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":48,"positioning":43,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":56,"awareness":58,"judgement":44},"picture":"Yuzuki Aikawa.png"},{"id":1267,"name":"Peter Avalon","realName":"Peter Avalon","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":49,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1989-06-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":10,"charisma":65,"micSkills":52,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"ability":57,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":59,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"Peter Avalon is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is one half of PPRay alongside Ray Rosas. He is best known for his work with AEW and NJoA.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Carson City, Nevada, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1267","wrestlerId":1267,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2023-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[631,1280,2155,2384],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":88,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":88,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":58,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":25,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":18,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":67,"awareness":56,"judgement":69},"picture":"Peter Avalon.png"},{"id":1269,"name":"Kenoh","realName":"Kenoh","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":45,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":209,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1985-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":7,"charisma":62,"micSkills":80,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100,"ability":75,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":69,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Daisuke Nakae is a Japanese professional wrestler, better known for his ring name Kenou. Nakae, a decorated nippon kempo practitioner, started his career in professional wrestling in the Michinoku Pro Wrestling Dojo, where he was introduced by Jinsei Shinzaki. He debuted in 2007 under the name of Kenou (?? Keno?, Fist King) and wrestled a number of exhibition and low-profile matches against fellow trainees Rui Hiugaji and Takayuki Aizawa. In late 2008, he was sent to Okinawa Pro Wrestling to hone his skills, adopting the name Kanmuriwashi Yoko and the gimmick of an afro kickboxer. In Septiember 2009, Kenou made his return to Michinoku Pro, shockingly beating Tohoku Junior Heavyweight Champion Fujita \"Jr.\" Hayato and capturing the title. He feuded with Hayato and his heel stable, Kowloon, and made alliances with the Michinoku Seikigun, slowly becoming the next ace of the promotion after Yoshitsune's departure.","alterEgos":["Daisuke Nakae"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1269","wrestlerId":1269,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2015-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":38400,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1000,4103,4104],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":82,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":75,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"picture":"Kenou.png"},{"id":1270,"name":"Robert King","realName":"Robert King","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":212,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1983-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":3,"charisma":82,"micSkills":69,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":60,"ability":75,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":66,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Robert King is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with NWA.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":0,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":0,"brandBuilding":0,"socialMediaSavvy":0,"ruleKnowledge":69,"positioning":55,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":45,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Robert King.png"},{"id":1271,"name":"Mike Chioda","realName":"Mike Chioda","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":176,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1966-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":12,"charisma":81,"micSkills":89,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":53,"ability":77,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":42,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Michael Joseph \"Mike\" Chioda is a senior referee who is currently signed to WWE. As a young man, Chioda lived close to the Marellas (Gorilla Monsoon and his son Joey), who helped him break into the wrestling business. Being trained as a referee, Chioda first began to appear in WWE in 1989, when it was known as the World Wrestling Federation (WWF), most notably at Survivor Series 1989. After taking a hiatus from refereeing following WrestleMania VII, he began to reappear on camera around 1993. Chioda has also competed in an actual wrestling match, teaming with Chris Jericho and The Rock to take on the team of The Dudley Boyz and referee Nick Patrick on an episode of SmackDown! in 2001.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":35,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":28,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":28,"brandBuilding":7,"socialMediaSavvy":23,"ruleKnowledge":85,"positioning":68,"reactionSpeed":35,"consistency":55,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Mike Chioda.png"},{"id":1272,"name":"Rod Zapata","realName":"Rod Zapata","nickname":"","type":"referee","promotionId":64,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":156,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1978-03-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":1,"charisma":81,"micSkills":64,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":60,"ability":77,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":60,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Rod Zapata is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with WWE.","alterEgo