ster as Rasse. He mainly uses a high-flying style. He has worked for many Japanese federations: after graduating in the 9th Toryumon school class term, he debuted in 2002 in Toryumon Mexico with the gimmick of Small Dandy Fuji, a little version of the Japanese wrestler Sumo Dandy Fujii, teaming up with SUWAcito and Mini CIMA, forming the Mini CMAX stable; he continued using this gimmick during 2003. He joined Michinoku Pro Wrestling, originally as Michinoku Ranger Silver with Michinoku Ranger Gold as his partner. He later changed his name and gimmick to Rasse, a masked character representing the Aomori Nebuta Matsuri, which he currently uses. Rasse gained a title shot for the Tohoku Tag Titles, teaming up with Shanao, and losing to Great Sasuke & Dick Togo, and lost the final match for the Tohoku Jr. Heavyweight Title to Takeshi Minamino.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3066,3101],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":74,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"picture":"Rasse.png"},{"id":1413,"name":"Savio Vega","realName":"Savio Vega","nickname":"","type":"scout","promotionId":5,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":260,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1964-08-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":10,"charisma":84,"micSkills":94,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":81,"injuryProne":87,"ability":78,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":41,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"A perennial main eventer in Puerto Rico, Vega is one of the island’s greatest brawlers known for his explosive spinning heel kick, jumping high kick and fighting spirit.\r\n\r\nVega lit up New York City in the mid 1990s teaming with Razor Ramon to form one of the most beloved tag teams of the era. However, many may know of Vega’s ultraviolet alter ego “TNT” who has caused havoc throughout the sport dating back decades.\r\n\r\nOne of the most decorated Caribbean grapplers in the history of the sport, Savio Vega has won countless championships in the Caribbean and has served as a general manager for Puerto Rico’s top organizations over the past few years.\r\n\r\nVega, who splits his time between San Juan, Puerto Rico and the South Bronx, serves as a player/coach in MLW where he mentors bluechip wrestlers while also rumbling in the ring on occasion.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Vega Alta, Puerto Rico","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2027-06-21T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1413","wrestlerId":1413,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2025-06-21T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-06-21T00:00:00.000Z","wage":20500,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":40,"productFit":40,"riskTaking":46,"matchLayout":40,"psychology":28,"workerManagement":29,"trainingIntensity":41,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":45,"teaching":21,"diagnosis":49,"rehabilitation":43,"prevention":42,"mediaHandling":43,"brandBuilding":28,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":47,"positioning":57,"reactionSpeed":24,"consistency":54,"awareness":43,"judgement":97},"picture":"Savio Vega.png"},{"id":1414,"name":"Kevin Keenan","realNa