,"popularity":6,"charisma":77,"micSkills":82,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":100,"ability":66,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":61,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Daisuke Sasaki is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with DDT.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1080,2892,3402],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":81,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":83,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":81,"consistency":76,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"picture":"Daisuke Sasaki.png"},{"id":1457,"name":"Danshoku Dino","realName":"Danshoku Dino","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":231,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1977-05-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":64,"micSkills":58,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"ability":53,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":41,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"comedy","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"counter","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Danshoku Dino is a Japanese professional wrestler. Dino plays an overly exaggerated homosexual character similar to the likes of Adrian Street. His ring name comes from the character Baron Dino from the manga series Sakigake!! Otokojuku. Dino was trained in shoot fighting prior to training to be a wrestler and he incorporated this training into his wrestling style. In addition to wrestling in Dramatic Dream Team (DDT), he has also competed in several independent wrestling promotions around Japan, including Dragon Gate, Ice Ribbon, Kaientai Dojo, Osaka Pro Wrestling and Pro Wrestling ZERO1-MAX. In February 2007, Dino made his first excursion overseas, as he debuted for a few American independent promotions such as Chikara, Combat Zone Wrestling (CZW) and International Wrestling Cartel (IWC).","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2688],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":80,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":20,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":70,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"picture":"Danshoku Dino.png"},{"id":1458,"name":"DJ Nira","realName":"DJ Nira","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1982-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":40,"micSkills":62,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":37,"injuryProne":98,"ability":62,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":53,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"comedy","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"counter","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"DJ Nira is K-DOJO's premier comedy wrestler, very rarely wrestling seriously. Nira was involved in a comedy feud with Kashiwa-gumi for much of 2004/2005. In 2005, after the GET and RAVE split, Nira was placed in RAVE and became the RAVE commentator on the Puroresu King shows. In 2006, for a month, he was taken under the wing of Boso Boy Raito and became Boso Boy Mild for a short time.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":40,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":28,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":55,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"picture":"DJ Nira.png"},{"id":1459,"name":"Gorgeous Matsuno","realName":"Gorgeous Matsuno","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":165,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1961-04-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":46,"micSkills":51,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":100,"ability":35,"currentAbility":16,"potentialAbility":18,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"comedy","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"counter","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Gorgeous Matsuno is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Comedy style. He is best known for his work with DDT.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":55,"productFit":80,"riskTaking":80,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":80,"trainingIntensity":51,"technicalCoaching":17,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":20,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":28,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":16,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":42,"awareness":56,"judgement":66},"picture":"Gorgeous Matsuno.png"},{"id":1460,"name":"Gota Ihashi","realName":"Gota Ihashi","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":243,"height":154,"dateOfBirth":"1983-11-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":59,"micSkills":59,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"ability":56,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":50,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"comedy","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"counter","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Gota Ihashi is a Japanese wrestler who has been wrestling in DDT as a comedy “fat clone” of Kota Ibushi for quite a long time before being officially introduced in the roster in June 2009.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":61,"productFit":88,"riskTaking":42,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":88,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":24,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":18,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":63,"awareness":58,"judgement":70},"picture":"Gota Ihashi.png"},{"id":1461,"name":"HARASHIMA","realName":"HARASHIMA","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":198,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1974-07-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":6,"charisma":73,"micSkills":62,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"ability":59,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":42,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"HARASHIMA is a Japanese professional wrestler. He originally debuted as Hero! in 2001 and twice won the KO-D Tag Team Championship with Kudo. He changed his name to Darkside Hero! in 2005 and won the KO-D Tag Team Championship with Toru Owashi. In 2006 he became Harashima, and beat Toru Owashi for the KO-D Openweight Championship on December 29, 2006. He first defended the Championship versus Daichi Kakimoto on January 28, 2007. He beat Kakimoto with his Somato finisher. His next title defence was on February 25, 2007, where he beat Danshoku Dieno. He then defended the KO-D Openweight Championship on April 1, 2007, beating Sanshiro Takagi. Harashima lost the KO-D Openweight Championship to Koo. In a rematch on October 21, 2007 he recovered the title, becoming a 2-time KO-D Openweight Champion. He defended the title 2 times: against Mikami on January 27, 2008 and against Yasu Urano on March 9, 2008. He lost the belt to Dick Togo in a 5-way match on May 6, 2008.","alterEgos":["HERO!"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1553,2437,2438,2439,2907],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":81,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":82,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":74,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":81,"consistency":86,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"picture":"HARASHIMA.png"},{"id":1462,"name":"Hoshitango","realName":"Hoshitango","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Other","gender":"M","weight":298,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1965-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":3,"charisma":57,"micSkills":64,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":95,"ability":47,"currentAbility":24,"potentialAbility":26,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hoshitango Imachi (born Imachi Marcelo Salomon) is an Argentine-born Japanese former professional sumo wrestler and current professional wrestler. His highest rank was Juryo 3. A former swimming instructor, Salomon joined Michinoku stable in May 1987. He was the first Jew in professional sumo. Hoshitango became a Japanese citizen in October 2000. His Japanese name was registered as Tango Hoshi. Imachi is currently a professional wrestler for the Japanese company DDT (Dramatic Dream Team) and has also wrestled for HUSTLE, Ice Ribbon and New Japan Pro Wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Argentina","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":52,"technicalCoaching":28,"characterCoaching":62,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":52,"consistency":56,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"picture":"Hoshitango.png"},{"id":1463,"name":"Kazuki Hirata","realName":"Kazuki Hirata","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":172,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1987-11-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":64,"micSkills":45,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"ability":51,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":50,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kazuki Hirata is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is best known for his work with DDT.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":78,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":76,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"picture":"Kazuki Hirata.png"},{"id":1464,"name":"Konosuke Takeshita","realName":"Konosuke Takeshita","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":231,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1995-05-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-08-18T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"popularity":45,"charisma":77,"micSkills":99,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":100,"ability":78,"currentAbility":78,"potentialAbility":96,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Debuted at the Nippon Budokan Tournament in August 2012 as an active high school wrestler. After graduating from high school, he entered the Nippon Sport Science University, worked hard to balance his studies and professional wrestling, and graduated in March 2018. The theme of his graduation thesis was \"German Suplex\". He set the record for most defenses of the KO-D Openweight Championship with 11, until he lost to Shigehiro Irie in April 2018. With his appearance on the cover of a weekly pro-wrestling magazine, expectations are high for him as a standard-bearer for the new era.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1091,2561,4212],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":81,"characterCoaching":74,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":85,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":86,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"picture":"Konosuke Takeshita.png","promotionId":76,"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1464","wrestlerId":1464,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2027-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wageType":"per-appearance","additionalContracts":[{"id":"tew-contract-1464-38","wrestlerId":1464,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false}],"alsoWorksFor":["NJPW"]},{"id":1465,"name":"KUDO","realName":"KUDO","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"M","w