","debut":"2002-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":42,"charisma":81,"micSkills":86,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"ability":76,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":89,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Malakai Black enters the ring with total composure and masterful precision, emerging from the quiet darkness just long enough to knock someone’s head off.\r\n\r\nTrained in kickboxing and the Indonesian martial art of pencak silat, the Dutch Superstar boasts a world-class arsenal of strikes, none more disruptive than his Black Mass spinning heel kick. MMA pioneer Bob Schrijber was among Black’s early mentors, and before coming to NXT in 2017, the head-rocking Superstar spent years dominating independent wrestling circuits around the globe.\r\n\r\nHis path of destruction carried into the black-and-gold brand, where he went undefeated in one-on-one competition for over a year before winning the NXT Championship at TakeOver: New Orleans.","alterEgos":["Malakai Black","Tommy End"],"birthplace":"Netherlands","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[411,592,1511,1512,1513,2622,2748,2857,3605],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":72,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":74,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":67,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"picture":"Tommy End_alt8.png"},{"id":1518,"name":"Michael Dante","realName":"Michael Dante","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base