lse,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yumiko Hotta is a Japanese professional wrestler and mixed martial artist. Hotta was trained by and started her career in the All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling (AJW) promotion in June 1985. She worked for the promotion until 2003, becoming a three-time WWWA World and WWWA World Tag Team Champion. In June 2003, Hotta took over the Hyper Visual Fighting Arsion promotion and renamed it Major Girl's Fighting AtoZ. Under Hotta's leadership, the promotion lasted only three years, before folding in 2006, after which Hotta became a freelancer. In January 2011, Hotta joined the new Universal Woman's Pro Wrestling Reina promotion, but just sixteen months later she announced that the promotion was folding. Afterwards, she affiliated herself with the World Woman Pro-Wrestling Diana promotion, becoming the leader of the villainous Bousou-gun stable.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":49,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":69,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":51,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":46,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":42,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Yumiko Hotta.png"},{"id":1776,"name":"Yumi Ohka","realName":"Yumi Ohka","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":130,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1979-04-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":58,"micSkills":47,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"ability":58,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":47,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yumiko Abe is a Japanese professional wrestler better known by the ring name Yumi Ohka. Originally trained by the now defunct JDStar promotion, Ohka now works for Oz Academy and Pro Wrestling Wave, where she is a former Wave Single and Wave Tag Team Champion. She is the managing director of Zabun Co., Ltd., which owns Pro Wrestling Wave.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1714,1716,1717,2480,2497],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":56,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":74,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Yumi Ohka.png"},{"id":1777,"name":"Shuu Shibutani","realName":"Shuu Shibutani","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":117,"height":154,"dateOfBirth":"1979-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":2,"charisma":68,"micSkills":65,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":81,"injuryProne":100,"ability":77,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kana Shibutani is a Japanese professional wrestler better known by the ring name Shuu Shibutani. Having started her career in the JDStar promotion in September 2004, Shibutani remained with the promotion until it folded in July 2007, after which she affiliated herself with Pro Wrestling Wave. She is a former one-time Wave Tag Team Champion.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":72,"awareness":51,"judgement":71},"picture":"Shuu Shibutani.png"},{"id":1778,"name":"Mima Shimoda","realName":"Mima Shimoda","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":143,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1970-12-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1987-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":6,"charisma":68,"micSkills":65,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"ability":57,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Mima Shimoda is a Japanese female professional wrestler, who is working for the Mexican professional wrestling promotion Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) and Japanese promotion World Woman Pro-Wrestling Diana. Shimoda trained in the All Japan Women's Dojo and was part of the \"class of 1987\" along with Manami Toyota, Toshiyo Yamada and Etsuko Mita. Shimoda was paired up with Toyota to form a tag team called The Sweethearts. In 2006 Shimoda moved to Mexico and began working regularly for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) as well as making frequent trips to Japan to work with a number of Japanese women's promotions, often touring with other CMLL wrestlers.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2989],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":62,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"picture":"Mima Shimoda.png"},{"id":1779,"name":"KAORU","realName":"KAORU","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":139,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1969-02-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":63,"micSkills":67,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"ability":70,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":40,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kaoru Maeda is a Japanese professional wrestler better known by the ring name Kaoru (stylized in all capital letters). Billed as the \"Original Hardcore Queen\", Kaoru is known for her wrestling style, which combines high-flying with hardcore wrestling. Trained by the All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling (AJW) promotion, Maeda worked in both Japan and Mexico in the late 80s and early 90s, before making her breakthrough in the Gaea Japan promotion, where she most notably was a founding member of the D-Fix stable. After the folding of Gaea Japan in 2005, Maeda became a freelancer, though closely affiliating herself with the Oz Academy promotion. After returning from a three-year-long injury break in March 2014, Maeda resumed working as a freelancer, before signing with the new Marvelous promotion in January 2015.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1724,2482,2507,3007,3008,3348],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":76,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":67,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"picture":"KAORU.png"},{"id":1781,"name":"Ronda Rousey","realName":"Ronda Rousey","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":134,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1987-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2018-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":57,"charisma":59,"micSkills":65,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"ability":63,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":83,"morale":"good","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"There have been Superstars who tried fighting and fighters who tried their hand at being Superstars. But there is only one Ronda Rousey.\r\n\r\nThis record-setting modern legend has blazed a trail through mixed-martial arts, beginning with a bronze medal showing in judo during the 2008 Beijing Summer Olympics and, most notably, continuing with a record-setting tear through UFC as the first female competitor to ever sign with the company. Given her status as the Strikeforce Women’s Bantamweight Champion before that promotion was absorbed by the UFC, Rousey was named the first-ever UFC Women’s Bantamweight Champion upon her arrival. It's no surprise that she was destined to become the first woman to be inducted into the UFC Hall of Fame on July of 2018.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3739],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":45,"storytelling":51,"productFit":13,"riskTaking":51,"matchLayout":53,"psychology":45,"workerManagement":13,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":49,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":87,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":3,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":35,"awareness":45,"judgement":32},"picture":"Ronda Rousey_alt4.png"},{"id":1782,"name":"Hideki Suzuki","realName":"Hideki Suzuki","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":3,"base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":249,"height":187,"dateOfBirth":"1980-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":51200,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":19,"charisma":76,"micSkills":77,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"ability":60,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hideki Suzuki is a Japanese wrestler who works in America and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Technician style. He is best known for his work with NOAH, NXT, BJW, ZERO1 and WRESTLE-1.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1782","wrestlerId":1782,"promotionId":3,"startDate":"2023-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":51200,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":87,"characterCoaching":46,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":46,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":19,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":76,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Hideki Suzuki_alt2.png"},{"id":1783,"name":"Sylvain Grenier","realName":"Sylvain Grenier","nickname":"","type":"trainer","base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":235,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1977-03-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":5,"charisma":87,"micSkills":87,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"ability":79,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Sylvain Grenier is a Canadian professional wrestler. He is best known for his appearances with World Wrestling Entertainment between 2003 and 2007 where he was part of La Résistance and became a four time World Tag Team Champion with René Duprée one time and Rob Conway three times. After his release from WWE, Grenier became a French language commentator for Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) Impact! for a number of years and continues to wrestle on the Québec independent circuit.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Canada","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1157,1158],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":20,"storytelling":46,"productFit":24,"riskTaking":53,"matchLayout":54,"psychology":50,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":59,"characterCoaching":89,"teaching":84,"diagnosis":42,"rehabilitation":48,"prevention":48,"mediaHandling":26,"brandBuilding":39,"socialMediaSavvy":52,"ruleKnowledge":50,"positioning":22,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":24,"awareness":21,"judgement":42},"picture":"Sylvain Grenier.png"},{"id":1784,"name":"Nanae Takahashi","realName":"Nanae Takahashi","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":143,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1978-12-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":7,"charisma":63,"micSkills":80,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":100,"ability":74,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":true,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Nanae Takahashi, a 1996 graduate of the Animal Hamaguchi Gym, is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. She is a Small worker who is classed as using a Technician style. She is best known for her work with Stardom, Marigold, GLEAT, ZERO1, Ice Ribbon and SEAdLINNNG.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1796,2508,3617,4030],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":70,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":71,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"picture":"Nanae Takahashi_alt3.png"},{"id":1785,"name":"Fuka","realName":"Fuka","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":110,"height":152,"dateOfBirth":"1984-08-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"popularity":3,"charisma":82,"micSkills":92,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":87,"ability":84,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":72,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Fuka Kakimoto s a Japanese retired professional wrestler, mixed martial artist and model better known simply as Fuka. She was trained by JDStar as part of the promotion's \"Athtress\" program and made her debut in February 2004, quickly garnering a large fan following. From 2005 to 2006, Fuka also fought three mixed martial arts fights, finishing with a record of two wins and one loss. During her years in JDStar, Fuka became the inaugural Princess of Pro-Wrestling (POP) Champion and also held the Princess of Ketsudeka (POK) and TWF World Tag Team Championships. After the promotion folded in July 2007, Fuka became a freelancer, while also starting to promote her own series of independent wrestling events under the banner of Fuka Matsuri (\"Fuka Festival\"). As a freelancer, Fuka also made several trips to Mexico, working for local independent promotions. Fuka ended her in-ring career in March 2010 at the age of 25, after which she began training wrestlers for the newly founded Stardom.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":44,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":65,"