, SEAdLINNNG, Marvelous and EVE. She is currently an AAAW Tag Team champion. She is the current booker of Marvelous. She is the protege of Chigusa Nagayo.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1701,2481,3011,3427],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":73,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":52,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":83,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"picture":"Takumi Iroha.png"},{"id":1799,"name":"Kaori Yoneyama","realName":"Kaori Yoneyama","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":128,"height":147,"dateOfBirth":"1981-02-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":10,"charisma":60,"micSkills":82,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":77,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Kaori Yoneyama is a Japanese wrestler who works in America and Japan. She is a Very Small worker who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. She is one half of RESET alongside Emi Sakura. She is best known for her work with DDT, BJW, STARDOM, Sendai Girls, WRESTLE-1, ZERO1, SHIMMER, OZ Academy, Ice Ribbon, SEAdLINNNG, FREEDOMS, EVE and CHIKARA. She is currently the OZ Academy Openweight champion.","alterEgos":["Death Yama-san","Gokigen Death","Otaku-chan"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2506,3611],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":75,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":64,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"picture":"Kaori Yoneyama_alt4.png"},{"id":1800,"name":"Hiroyo Matsumoto","realName":"Hiroyo Matsumoto","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":154,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1985-11-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":7,"charisma":83,"micSkills":88,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":100,"ability":79,"currentAbility":79,"potentialAbility":82,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hiroyo Matsumoto is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada and Japan. She is a Small worker who is classed as using a Brawler style. She is best known for her work with Ice Ribbon, Sendai Girls, SEAdLINNNG and OZ Academy.","alterEgos":["BINGO"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[661,1711,1957,2483,2484,2987,2988],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":59,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":48,"awareness":72,"judgement":83},"picture":"Hiroyo Matsumoto_alt2.png"},{"id":1801,"name":"Tsubasa Kuragaki","realName":"Tsubasa Kuragaki","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":174,"height":160,"dateOfBirth":"1975-12-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":4,"charisma":47,"micSkills":46,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":45,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yasuko Kuragaki is a Japanese professional wrestler better known by the ring name Tsubasa Kuragaki. For most of her career, Kuragaki has worked for JWP Joshi Puroresu, becoming a one-time JWP Junior and two-time JWP Openweight Champion as a singles wrestler. As a tag team wrestler, she is best known as one half of the \"Harukura\" tag team with Kayoko Haruyama, with whom she has held the Daily Sports Women's and JWP Tag Team Championships three times each. She quit JWP in October 2013 to become a freelancer. She is currently working most notably for Oz Academy.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":57,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":35,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":53,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Tsubasa Kuragaki.png"},{"id":1803,"name":"Meiko Satomura","realName":"Meiko Satomura","nickname":"","type":"scout","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":150,"height":154,"dateOfBirth":"1979-11-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"popularity":29,"charisma":80,"micSkills":91,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":100,"ability":100,"currentAbility":77,"potentialAbility":77,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Meiko Satomura is a Japanese professional wrestler. She co-founded Sendai Girls' Pro Wrestling alongside Jinsei Shinzaki. She is a 2 time AAAW Singles Champion, a 2 time AAAW Tag Team Champion (with Ayako Hamada) and a 1 time AAAW Junior Heavyweight Tag Team Champion (with Sonoko Kato). Meiko has also trained several current female wrestlers, including Dash Chisako and Sendai Sachiko.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2842,2843],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":50,"productFit":38,"riskTaking":47,"matchLayout":29,"psychology":21,"workerManagement":49,"trainingIntensity":40,"technicalCoaching":22,"characterCoaching":35,"teaching":59,"diagnosis":30,"rehabilitation":42,"prevention":43,"mediaHandling":25,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":37,"ruleKnowledge":44,"positioning":37,"reactionSpeed":26,"consistency":23,"awareness":23,"judgement":91},"picture":"Meiko Satomura_alt2.png"},{"id":1804,"name":"Mayumi Ozaki","realName":"Mayumi Ozaki","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":125,"height":154,"dateOfBirth":"1968-10-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":6,"charisma":57,"micSkills":69,"condition":63,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"ability":63,"currentAbility":35,"potentialAbility":37,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"submission","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Mayumi Ozaki is a Japanese female professional wrestler. Ozaki debuted in a tag match in August, 1986.[2] In her career, she held the WWWA tag titles with Dynamite Kansai from April 11, 1993 to December 6, 1993 (both winning from and losing to Manami Toyota and Toshiyo Yamada of All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling (AJW). She also held the UWA Junior and JWP Junior titles between 1988 and 1991, and teamed with Cuty Suzuki and Hikari Fukuoka to win the JWP Tag Titles a number of times between 1992 and 1995. Most recently, she held the AAAW Tag Team Championship with Aja Kong, beating GAEA's Sugar Sato and Chikayo Nagashima on August 23, 1998 in Tokyo. In December 2011, Ozaki took part in American promotion Chikara's JoshiMania weekend, teaming with Mio Shirai in a losing effort against the team of Cherry and Ayako Hamada on night one on December 2.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1713,1714,1715,2507,3007,3008],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":87,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":79,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":65,"awareness":85,"judgement":91},"picture":"Mayumi Ozaki.png"},{"id":1805,"name":"Chigusa Nagayo","realName":"Chigusa Nagayo","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":192,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1964-12-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1980-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":7,"charisma":70,"micSkills":58,"condition":55,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":98,"ability":57,"currentAbility":28,"potentialAbility":40,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Chigusa Nagayo is a retired Japanese female professional wrestler best known for her mainstream popularity in the 1980s as a member of the tag team The Crush Gals with long-time partner Lioness Asuka. She was the founder of the GAEA Women's Professional Wrestling organization (known simply as GAEA). She briefly competed as alter-ego Lady Zero in GAEA. Nagayo appears in the 2000 documentary Gaea Girls. Following her retirement, Nagayo began producing her own independent events and founded Marvelous That's Women Pro Wrestling in 2015.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":57,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":45,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"picture":"Chigusa Nagayo.png"},{"id":1807,"name":"Miyako Matsumoto","realName":"Miyako Matsumoto","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":119,"height":160,"dateOfBirth":"1985-04-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":2,"charisma":52,"micSkills":49,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"ability":51,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":48,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Miyako Matsumoto  is a Japanese professional wrestler and actress. She is the founder, owner and promoter of the Gake no Fuchi Puroresu promotion and currently also works for Ice Ribbon, where she is a former one-time ICE×60, three-time Triangle Ribbon Champion and a two-time International Ribbon Tag Team Champion, making her Ice Ribbon's second Triple Crown Champion. She also wrestles regularly for Oz Academy and Reina Joshi Puroresu.","alterEgos":["Daemon Miyako","Fighting Matsumoto"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3254,3255],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":64,"productFit":85,"riskTaking":35,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":85,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":59,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":65,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":17,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":82,"awareness":58,"judgement":69},"picture":"Miyako Matsumoto.png"},{"id":1808,"name":"Command Bolshoi","realName":"Command Bolshoi","nickname":"","type":"writer","base":"Japan","gender":"F","weight":106,"height":144,"dateOfBirth":"1974-11-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"popularity":6,"charisma":93,"micSkills":90,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":87,"ability":79,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Command Bolshoi  is a Japanese professional wrestler. She currently works as the president of JWP Joshi Puroresu promotion, where she is a former one-time JWP Openweight Champion, a six-time JWP Tag Team Champion and a three-time Daily Sports Women's Tag Team Champion. Bolshoi has worked under mask for a majority of her career and has managed to keep her real name, birthday and birthplace secret.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3347],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":51,"technicalCoaching":82,"characterCoaching":69,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":58,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Command Bolshoi.png"},{"id":1809,"name":"Ash by Elegance","realName":"Ash by Elegance","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":28,"base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":125,"height":157,"dateOfBirth":"1988-11-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":28,"charisma":51,"micSkills":57,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"ability":58,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":63,"morale":"poor","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Ash by Elegance, who graduated from WWE Performance Center on 01 September 2014, is an American wrestler who works in the USA and Canada. She is a 5'3\", 125lb worker who is classed as using a Regular style. She uses the Samoan Driver as her finisher. She is best known for her work with WWE, TNA and NXT.","alterEgos":["Dana Brooke"],"birthplace":"Seven Hills, Ohio, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1809","wrestlerId":1809,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":30700,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[995,2074,2339,3797],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":54,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":65,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"picture":"Ash by Elegance.png"},{"id":1810,"name":"Carmella","realName":"Carmella","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"F","weight":110,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1987-10-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":42,"charisma":39,"micSkills":52,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"ability":51,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":46,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"By reading her background on paper, you’d be forgiven if you assumed that Carmella was never going to make it in WWE. A former Laker girl who found her first success as the third wheel of a boys’ club with two of NXT’s most popular stars, the so-called “Princess of Staten Island” seemed destined for a steady, if unremarkable, career when she was chosen as the very last pick of the 2016 WWE Draft to fill out SmackDown LIVE’s Women’s division.\r\n\r\nHow wrong those assumptions would have been. In just a couple of short years, Carmella’s résumé expanded at lightning speeds. She won the first-ever Women’s Money in the Bank Match (and the second), defeated no less a talent than Charlotte Flair to win the SmackDown Women’s Championship, and won the second-ever WrestleMania Women’s Battle Royal. Her competitiveness is matched only by her creativity, which exploded in the freewheeling sideshow of the Mixed Match Challenge, where she joined forces with R-Truth.","alterEgos":["Leah Van Dale"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2074],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":56,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":70,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":70,"awareness":53,"judgement":72},"picture":"Carmella_alt8.png"},{"id":1811,"name":"Cash Wheeler","realName":"Cash Wheeler","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":207,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1987-05-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":48,"charisma":78,"micSkills":90,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"ability":74,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":78,"morale":"fair","presentation":"heel","prestige":"mid","style":"technical","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Daniel Marshall Wheeler is an American worker from North Carolina best known for his time in WWE under the name Dash Wilder, where he teamed with Scott Dawson as The Revival. Their old school 80s style of tag team wrestling led to them being compared favourably with The Brain Busters (Arn Anderson & Tully Blanchard) and they gained a reputation for having consistently great matches while in NXT. Despite becoming 3-time tag team champions after being called up to the main roster in 2017, they were plagued by poor booking and had multiple requests for their release turned down before finally being let go in April 2020. The former Dash now goes by the name Cash Wheeler and continues to team with Dawson, now named Dax Harwood, under the name \"FTR\" - a reference to their online feud with The Young Bucks through their web series Being The Elite.","alterEgos":["Dash"],"birthplace":"Asheville, North Carolina, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1811","wrestlerId":1811,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1494,1495,1592,2048,2077,3502,3590,3641],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":57,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":88,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"picture":"Cash Wheeler.png"},{"id":1812,"name":"Rich Bocchini","realName":"Rich Bocchini","nickname":"","type":"commentator","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":158,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1980-03-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1500,"popularity":1,"charisma":69,"micSkills":72,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":74,"injuryProne":66,"ability":67,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":55,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Rich Bocchini is a play-by-play commentator for Major League Wrestling, since MLW: One-Shot in 2017.\r\n\r\nHe is a TV and radio play-by-play announcer, known primarily through his work in professional hockey as well as professional wrestling.\r\n\r\nRich appeared on WWE television programming  and his voice was the soundtrack for many of the cornerstone moments of WWE’s NXT brand. He served as the play-by-play voice of SmackDown, Main Event and Superstars and had the honor of calling the action from ringside at Madison Square Garden for the WWE Network’s first live special from the storied arena. In addition to his on-air work, Rich also worked behind the scenes at the WWE Performance Center and in production at NXT live events.","alterEgos":["Rich Brennan"],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":37,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":37,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":37,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Rich Brennan.png"},{"id":1817,"name":"Wild Boar","realName":"Wild Boar","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":205,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1989-10-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":60,"micSkills":65,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"ability":50,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":52,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"striker","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"strike","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Wild Boar is an animalistic competitor who has stalked his prey across the United Kingdom, Norway and Spain as both a singles competitor and tag team specialist. With unnerving black eyes, the unhinged self-proclaimed “Welsh Wrestler-Man” is as vicious as they come, with as little restraint inside the squared circle as he has teeth in his head (many of his pearly whites were knocked out in a bar fight against four other men, in which he refused to go down).\r\n\r\nLike the snorting creature he emulates, Wild Boar is not someone to turn your back on, as he possesses the ability to ram through an opponent in the corner, hurl them over his head at high velocity or just ground them into submission.\r\n\r\nNXT UK has been warned. Wild Boar is loose and coming for you.","alterEgos":["Mike Hitchman"],"birthplace":"Wales","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1632,1801,1893,3247,3248],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":57,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":49,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":70,"awareness":51,"judgement":71},"picture":"Wild Boar.png"},{"id":1820,"name":"James Oxtoby","realName":"James Oxtoby","nickname":"","type":"referee","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":15