":29,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"poor","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"Cassie Lee, who graduated from Pro Wrestling Academy on 01 February 2009, is an Australian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada and Oceania. She is a 5'7\", 132lb worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. She uses the Bitch Kick, the Huracanrana and the Leg Sweep DDT as her finishers. She is one half of The IInspiration alongside Jessie McKay. She is best known for her work with WWE, TNA, NXT, PWA, MCW, SHIMMER and WR. She is married to Shawn Spears. She is the protege of Lance Storm.","alterEgos":["Peyton Royce","KC Cassidy"],"birthplace":"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1885","wrestlerId":1885,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2026-02-15T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":32800,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1742,2435,2436,3069,4140,4347],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":43,"storytelling":44,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":44,"psychology":43,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":24,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":48,"awareness":43,"judgement":66},"picture":"Peyton Royce_alt16.png"},{"id":1899,"name":"Trent Seven","realName":"Trent Seven","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":209,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1981-09-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":15,"charisma":86,"micSkills":70,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":83,"injuryProne":100,"ability":73,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":75,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"upper","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Distinguished yet dangerous, Trent Seven is like a character from the underworld of a Guy Ritchie film. His debonair appearance and charming manner of speech belie his gritty, hard-nosed approach to the ring. It’s that same competitive spirit that made Seven one of the United Kingdom’s top grapplers in the first place.\r\n\r\nAfter spending years collecting titles in the British independent scene, Seven landed on the radar of the WWE Universe during the WWE UK Championship Tournament in January 2017. Though he fell short of claiming the UK crown, The Don’s intelligent, hard-hitting offense made everyone take notice. A bastion of British Strong Style — an exciting, post-modern take on classic English wrestling traditions — Seven has since made frequent appearances in NXT, often teaming with fellow British Strong Style proponent Tyler Bate as Moustache Mountain.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"England","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[966,967,1237,1238,1846,2062,2195,3855],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":68,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":75,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"picture":"Trent Seven_alt8.png"},{"id":1900,"name":"Bravo Americano","realName":"Tyler Bate","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":174,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1997-03-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":38,"charisma":88,"micSkills":86,"condition":95,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":100,"ability":75,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":84,"morale":"fair","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"The first-ever United Kingdom Champion has made his way to NXT UK, ready to take his already prestigious career to the next level against to top Superstars from the UK and Ireland. Translation, the NXT UK locker room should definitely be concerned.\r\n\r\nWith experience in promotions like Fight Club Pro, PROGRESS and Chikara, Tyler Bate, who hails from Dudley, England, spent his formative years inside the ring inspired by one of the more eclectic groups you’ll ever hear - Johnny Saint, Steve Grey and The Big Red Monster, Kane.\r\n\r\nBate honed his craft while earning his daily quid as a forklift operator to pay the bills. A technically sound wrestler who prefers things fair but isn’t afraid to get down and dirty, Textbook Tyler fought his way through four opponents in the WWE United Kingdom Championship Tournament in 2017 — including the vicious Pete Dunne in the Finals — to become the first WWE United Kingdom Champion at age 19. And if he made history as a teenager, imagine what the fu","alterEgos":["Tyler Bate"],"birthplace":"Dudley, West Midlands, England","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1900","wrestlerId":1900,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[790,1237,1238,1846,2062,2195,3885,4370],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":62,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":57,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":70,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"picture":"Bravo Americano.png"},{"id":1901,"name":"Stephen Amell","realName":"Stephen Amell","nickname":"","type":"manager","base":"Canada","gender":"M","weight":210,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1981-05-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":31,"charisma":35,"micSkills":48,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"ability":51,"currentAbility":41,"potentialAbility":41,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Stephen Amell  is a Canadian actor. He is best known for portraying Oliver Queen / Green Arrow in the television series Arrow and will portray Casey Jones in the sequel to Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles. He is a huge WWE fan.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Canada","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":36,"storytelling":38,"productFit":1,"riskTaking":44,"matchLayout":39,"psychology":36,"workerManagement":1,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":31,"characterCoaching":62,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":56,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":65,"soc