ked for various promotions across Japan, including Wrestle-1, All Japan Pro Wrestling and ZERO-1.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":60,"productFit":79,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":79,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":49,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":28,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":16,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":64,"awareness":55,"judgement":65},"picture":"Koji Doi.png"},{"id":1990,"name":"Nia Jax","realName":"Nia Jax","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":64,"base":"Australia","gender":"F","weight":240,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1984-05-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","popularity":45,"charisma":53,"micSkills":77,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"ability":62,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":75,"morale":"fair","presentation":"heel","prestige":"mid","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"There’s one thing that’s painfully clear when someone steps in the ring with Nia Jax: She’s not like most women. The 6-foot-tall Jax has towered over other women for as long as she can recall. She was kicked out of activities like karate, kickboxing and judo as a child because someone always ended up getting hurt at her hands. Though Jax eventually turned her attention toward the world of modeling, she still hungered for competition. A cousin of The Rock, she made her way to the WWE Performance Center where she learned to harness her aggression in the squared circle. She immediately blew away all other Superstars in terms of power, claiming all of the WWE Performance Center’s female lifting records.","alterEgos":["Lina Fanene"],"birthplace":"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1990","wrestlerId":1990,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2023-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":50000,"wageType":"monthly","type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2340,2771,4284],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":53,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":12,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":73,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"picture":"Nia Jax.png"},{"id":1992,"name":"Kuuga","realName":"Kuuga","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":220,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1976-01-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":1,"charisma":57,"micSkills":44,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":36,"injuryProne":100,"ability":45,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":34,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Koji Nishimoto is a Japanese professional wrestler, better known by the ring names, Asian Cougar, Kappa Boy and Kuuga. Nishimoto got his start as a trainee under the Universal Pro-Wrestling, but the promotion fell under before he could make his professional debut. He would make his debut 4 years later in October of 1995 in the SPWF. He would become a masked wrestler as the Asian Cooger and would team with Asian Condor as they took on Hosei Fujita and Masamitsu Takatomu.","alterEgos":["Asian Cougar"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":41,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":41,"brandBuilding":28,"socialMediaSavvy":34,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":63,"awareness":59,"judgement":75},"picture":"Kuuga.png"},{"id":1994,"name":"Super Sasadango Machine","realName":"Yoshihiro Sakai","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":257,"height":180,"dateOfBirth":"1977-11-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":5,"charisma":59,"micSkills":58,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":95,"ability":46,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Muscle Sakai  is a Japanese professional wrestler who wrestled primarily in comedy matches for the Japanese wrestling promotion, Dramatic Dream Team and its sister promotions.","alterEgos":["Yoshihiro Sakai","Muscle Sakai"],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":62,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":50,"characterCoa