kings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Negro Navarro  is the ring name of Miguel Calderón Navarro, a Mexican luchador, or professional wrestler. Navarro works as a Freelancer on the Mexican independent circuit as well as making regular appearances for International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG). Navarro often teams with his sons, who are known as Trauma I and Trauma II. Negro Navarro was part of Los Misioneros de la Muerte (\"The Missionaries of Death\") with El Signo and El Texano; a team that is credited with popularizing the Trios match in Mexico to the point that it became the most common match for Trios teams in Mexican Lucha Libre.","alterEgos":["Último Vampiro"],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":89,"storytelling":92,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":3,"matchLayout":93,"psychology":89,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":48,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":60,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":97,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":48,"consistency":68,"awareness":89,"judgement":93},"picture":"Negro Navarro.png"},{"id":2268,"name":"Sean Maluta","realName":"Sean Maluta","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":191,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1988-09-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":2,"charisma":52,"micSkills":61,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"ability":49,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":50,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"The nephew of WWE Hall of Famer Afa, Maluta is a speedy grappler specializing in striking. One of his go-to maneuvers is a savate kick that can render any opponent unconscious. Strikes aren’t the only way he can win a match though. Maluta is not afraid to take flight and come crashing down on the opposition.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2533,3288],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":59,"productFit":48,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":48,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":52,"characterCoaching":42,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":42,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":73,"awareness":55,"judgement":52},"picture":"Sean Maluta.png"},{"id":2269,"name":"Ariya Daivari","realName":"Ariya Daivari","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":49,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":191,"height":175,"dateOfBirth":"1989-04-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":15,"charisma":74,"micSkills":62,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"ability":57,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":59,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"Since its inception, there has been one constant on 205 Live: Ariya Daivari touting his own greatness.\r\n\r\nNever shy about flaunting his money or looking down his nose at his fellow Cruiserweights, Daivari has engaged in memorable rivalries on the purple brand, colliding with the likes of Tony Nese, The Lucha House Party and Cedric Alexander.\r\n\r\nDespite his arrogance, Daivari tends to back up his words more often than not, as he has frequently put $10,000 of his own money on the line against local competitors in Daivari’s Dinero Division, and he has yet to taste defeat while doing so.","alterEgos":["Mustafa Bashir"],"birthplace":"Plymouth, Minnesota, United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2269","wrestlerId":2269,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2022-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[748,1502,3018,3566,3567,3574],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":52,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":80,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"Ariya Daivari.png"},{"id":2270,"name":"Oficial Spartan","realName":"Oficial Spartan","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":216,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1975-07-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":2,"charisma":55,"micSkills":79,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"ability":71,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":51,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Oficial Spartan is the current ring name of Victor Manuel Montés. In 2002 Super Mega left IWRG to work for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), leaving Los Megas (Mega and Ultra Mega) without a third man. Victor Montés was repackaged, given a new mask and suit that matched the other Megas and made his debut as \"Omega\". Not long after the replacement Los Megas won the IWRG Intercontinental Trios Championship from NOZAWA, Takemura and Masada. It has not been confirmed what Montés did between ending his stint as Omega and returning to IWRG in 2009, he could have been working as another masked character or even not worked in wrestling in that period of time. Montés returned to IWRG as the masked character \"Arlequín Rojo\". In the mid-2011 the group Los Oficiales introduced a new member called Oficial Spartans, later shortened to just Oficial Spartan, who was played by Montés and was brought in to replace the injured Oficial AK-47.","alterEgos":["Omega"],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":51,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":82,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"picture":"Spartan.png"},{"id":2272,"name":"Oficial Factor","realName":"Oficial Factor","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":225,"height":177,"dateOfBirth":"1977-11-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":65,"micSkills":61,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":100,"ability":64,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":49,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Cesar Caballero is a part of the Los Oficiales Elite group alongside Oficial Rayan and Oficial Spartan. Caballero previously worked under a number of other ring names including Mega, but they are not officially acknowledged, as the enmascarado character is promoted as a separate entity from his previous characters, which is often the case when a Mexican wrestler adopts a new masked character. In 2001 International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) formed a new \"trio\" known as Los Megas, taking three of their regular competitors, putting them together with a character based on the Mega character. Los Megas portrayed a kid-friendly técnico (good guys) group. In late 2011 Oficial Spartan and Oficial Rayan formed Los Oficiales Elite, a group created to rival Los Oficiales (Oficial 911, Oficial AK-47, and Oficial Fierro). In early 2012 Los Oficiales Elite became a trio with the introduction of Oficial Factor to the team. Factor was the returning Caballero under a new mask and ring character","alterEgos":["Mega"],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3259],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":55,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":77,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"picture":"Factor.png"},{"id":2273,"name":"Oficial 911","realName":"Oficial 911","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":185,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1981-02-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":45,"micSkills":66,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"ability":69,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":58,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"José Ángel Bocanegra González began wrestling in 2001, although it has never been publicly acknowledged which ring name he used at the time. In Mexico it is not unusual for wrestlers to gain in-ring experience under a generic enmascarado (masked) character early in their careers. In 2003 he adopted the enmascarado character \"Comando Mega\" in International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG), the name under which he first gained in-ring success. Comando Mega teamed up with Comando Gama and Comando Omega as the \"arch enemies\" of an IWRG técnico (good guy) group called Los Megas. In early 2007 IWRG officials decided to form a new version of the group Los Oficiales (\"The Officials\"), a masked trios group that all had a \"Police officer\" ring character. The three masked men, Oficial 911, Oficial AK-47 and Oficial Fierro were unveiled at a Lucha Libre festival in May 2007.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2378],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":69,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":67,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"picture":"Oficial 911.png"},{"id":2274,"name":"Oficial AK-47","realName":"Oficial AK-47","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":189,"height":172,"dateOfBirth":"1986-02-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":78,"micSkills":66,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"ability":75,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":71,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Mario Pardo Villagómez is a Mexican luchador, best known under the ring name Oficial AK-47. As Oficial AK-47 he is part of a group called Los Oficiales that has worked for International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) since 2007. Pardo made his debut in 2003, working as an enmascarado called \"Sureño de la Muerte\" (Spanish for \"Southern Death\"). Later on he was recast as \"Black Stone\", working on the undercard of various International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) shows.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[2378],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":67,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":66,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"picture":"Oficial AK47.png"},{"id":2275,"name":"Oficial Fierro","realName":"Oficial Fierro","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":183,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1974-04-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":3,"charisma":69,"micSkills":62,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":96,"ability":51,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":36,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Fernando Montes is a Mexican luchador, or professional wrestler, best known under the ring name Oficial Fierro. As Oficial Fierro he is part of a group called Los Oficiales that has worked for International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) since 2007. Fernando Montes made his professional wrestling debut in 1997, although it has never been publicly acknowledge which ring name he used at the time. In Mexico it is not unusual for wrestlers to gain in-ring experience under a generic enmascarado (masked) character early in their careers. In 1999 and 2000 he wrestled as \"Mercurio\", a low ranking enmascarado character in International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG). In 2000 he was repackaged as \"El Millonario\", a character patterned after Ted DiBiase's \"Million Dollar Man\" character from the World Wrestling Federation.","alterEgos":["Ultra Mega"],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":57,"characterCoaching":49,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":23,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":53,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"picture":"Oficial Fierro.png"},{"id":2276,"name":"Dr. Cerebro","realName":"Dr. Cerebro","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Mexico","gender":"M","weight":200,"height":165,"dateOfBirth":"1972-05-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":3000,"popularity":2,"charisma":60,"micSkills":65,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":100,"ability":72,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":47,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Alejandro Jiménez Cruz is a Mexican luchador, or professional wrestler best known under the ring name Dr. Cerebro (Spanish for \"Doctor Brain\"). He has been associated with the Mexican professional wrestling promotion International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) since his debut in 1996 and has portrayed both a tecnico (\"Good guy\") and a Rudo (\"bad guy\") wrestling character. He is also a licensed Chiropractor.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Mexico","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":70,"characterCoaching":64,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":78,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"picture":"Dr Cerebro.png"},{"id":2277,"name":"Keith Lee","realName":"Keith Lee","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":76,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":332,"height":185,"dateOfBirth":"1984-11-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":43,"charisma":22,"micSkills":38,"condition":68,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"ability":25,"currentAbility":25,"potentialAbility":85,"morale":"fair","presentation":"face","prestige":"mid","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Keith Lee is an American wrestler who works in America, the British Isles and Europe. He is a Heavyweight who is classed as using a Powerhouse style. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NXT, PWG, ROH and EVOLVE. He is married to Mia Yim.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2277","wrestlerId":2277,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":60000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1281,3350,3351,3515,3689],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":73,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":82,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"picture":"Keith Lee.png"},{"id":2278,"name":"Shane Taylor","realName":"Shane Taylor","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","promotionId":49,"base":"USA","gender":"M","weight":315,"height":182,"dateOfBirth":"1985-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","popularity":16,"charisma":65,"micSkills":56,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"ability":58,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":61,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"powerhouse","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":true,"story":"Shane Taylor was surrounded by violence while growing up on the mean streets of East Cleveland, and he brought a violent demeanor and survive-at-all-costs mentality when he came to Ring of Honor in 2016. The massive Taylor first wreaked havoc in the tag team division, and he later served as the enforcer of The Rebellion, a faction that included Kenny King, Rhett Titus and Caprice Coleman. After The Rebellion was forced to disband due to a match stipulation, Taylor has become even more dangerous -- especially if the price is right.\r\n\r\nAs Taylor continues to rise up the ranks in singles competition, he’s made it clear to everyone in the ROH locker room that if anyone needs a “problem solver,” he’s the man for the job.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"United States","managerId":0,"contractExpiryDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2278","wrestlerId":2278,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2024-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":16400,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false},"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[1281,3350,3351],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":61,"technicalCoaching":32,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":61,"consistency":73,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"picture":"Shane Taylor.png","additionalContracts":[{"id":"tew-contract-2278-76","wrestlerId":2278,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":40000,"wageType":"per-appearance","type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","bookingsPerMonth":4,"autoRenew":false}],"alsoWorksF