":"Chicano.png"},{"id":2381,"name":"Yusuke Kodama","realName":"Yusuke Kodama","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"Japan","gender":"M","weight":172,"height":170,"dateOfBirth":"1987-04-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4166,"popularity":4,"charisma":68,"micSkills":68,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"ability":65,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":63,"morale":"broken","presentation":"heel","prestige":"low","style":"high flyer","cardPosition":"mid","finisher":"","finisherType":"aerial","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Yusuke Kodama was trained by TAJIRI and was set to debut in Hustle in September 2009; unfortunately, HUSTLE was forced to cancel all the upcoming shows due to economic issues, so Kodama followed TAJIRI to the newborn Smash. Kodama made his professional wrestling debut on April 23, 2010, at SMASH 2, against Hajime Ohara and lost. As is customary for most professional wrestlers, Kodama spent most of his matches losing to other, more experienced wrestlers, which would help put over other wrestlers while at the same time give Kodama some in-ring, televised, experience. Kodama made his Wrestle-1 debut on June 27, 2014, defeating Hiroki Murase in a singles match.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Japan","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":75,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":75,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":65,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":41,"socialMediaSavvy":52,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":15,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":77,"awareness":62,"judgement":67},"picture":"Yusuke Kodama.png"},{"id":2383,"name":"Isla Dawn","realName":"Isla Dawn","nickname":"","type":"wrestler","base":"UK","gender":"F","weight":150,"height":167,"dateOfBirth":"1994-02-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":37500,"popularity":28,"charisma":63,"micSkills":45,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":93,"ability":52,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":80,"morale":"poor","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"technical","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"submission","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"“Unique” gets thrown around quite a bit in the world of sports-entertainment, but it’s safe to say that NXT UK has seen few competitors as singular as Isla Dawn.\r\n\r\nThis self-described “modern-day witch” employs a hard-hitting style drawing from her background in kickboxing and dance that has carried her throughout promotions across Europe.\r\n\r\nMolded by influences as varying as Goldust (her first WWE action figure) and Killian Dain (who saw her act in a play and encouraged her to begin wrestling training), Dawn is also unique in what she exemplifies: “A representation of all women, in all stages of their life and the power they hold.” Motivated by modern feminist ideals, Dawn also claims she represents “Never being what ‘a woman should be’ by societal standards.” She’s come to the right place.","alterEgos":[],"birthplace":"Scotland","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[3718,3726],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":49,"storytelling":54,"productFit":42,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":49,"workerManagement":42,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":56,"teaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":8,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":67,"awareness":49,"judgement":46},"pict