in Egan","nickname":"","type":"commentator","base":"UK","gender":"M","weight":160,"height":162,"dateOfBirth":"1985-05-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2021-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":66000,"popularity":9,"charisma":36,"micSkills":16,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":21,"injuryProne":0,"ability":33,"currentAbility":29,"potentialAbility":32,"morale":"broken","presentation":"face","prestige":"low","style":"all rounder","cardPosition":"lower","finisher":"","finisherType":"power","character":"","acceptsIndieBookings":false,"masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"inDevelopment":false,"story":"Hailing from Dublin, Ireland, Kevin Egan started his career in the entertainment industry with RTE, Ireland’s National Broadcaster, where he worked on world-class soccer events and the 2004 Olympics. Since moving to the United States in 2009, he has worked for the likes of Big Ten Network, the Chicago Fire Soccer Club, beIN SPORTS, CNN International and Sirius XM.\r\n\r\nEgan arrived in WWE in March of 2021, being introduced to the WWE Universe by his fellow backstage colleague, Sarah Schreiber, just a few hours ahead of making his Monday Night Raw debut as Kevin Patrick. He quickly became a fixture every Monday night, not only on Raw, but as the regular co-host of Raw Talk, often times paired with on-again, off-again 24/7 Champion R-Truth.","alterEgos":["Kevin Patrick"],"birthplace":"Ireland","managerId":0,"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"teams":[],"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":52,"teaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"picture":"Kevin Patrick.png"},{"id":4293,"name":"Sudu Upadhyay